    "path": "anthropic_claude/api_reference.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "| Endpoint | Maximum request size |\n|---|---|\n| Messages, Token Counting | 32 MB |\n| Message Batches API | 256 MB |\n| Files API | 500 MB |\n| Sessions, Agents, Environments | 32 MB |\nIf you exceed these limits, you'll receive a 413 request_too_large error.\nPartner-operated platforms have their own request size limits: Bedrock limits requests to 20 MB, and Google Cloud limits requests to 30 MB. Claude Platform on AWS uses the same limits as the direct Claude API. Consult your platform's documentation for current values.\nThe Claude API includes the following headers in every response:\nrequest-id: A globally unique identifier for the requestanthropic-organization-id: The organization ID associated with the API key used in the request\nClaude Platform on AWS adds an AWS request ID (x-amzn-requestid) alongside the standard request-id header. See Request IDs for the dual-ID handling pattern.",
    "character_count": 896
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2efb0143-6e64-4c1f-9a49-b567e97f1862",
    "technology": "Anthropic Claude",
    "technology_id": "source-anthropic-claude",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Anthropic",
