    "url": "https://docs.anthropic.com/en/release-notes/overview",
    "path": "anthropic_claude/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 53,
    "text": "- We've launched the MCP connector in public beta, a feature that allows you to connect to remote MCP servers directly from the Messages API.\n- To increase answer quality and decrease tool errors, we've changed the default value for the top_p nucleus sampling parameter in the Messages API from 0.999 to 0.99 for all models. To revert this change, settop_p to 0.999.\nAdditionally, when extended thinking is enabled, you can now settop_p to values between 0.95 and 1.\n- We've moved our Go SDK from beta to GA.\n- We've included minute and hour level granularity to the Usage page of Console alongside 429 error rates on the Usage page.\n- We've moved our Ruby SDK from beta to GA.\n- We've launched a web search tool in the API, allowing Claude to access up-to-date information from the web. Learn more in Web search tool.",
    "character_count": 818
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "235d1fe2-31a8-4a85-aee1-d862dc785646",
