    "path": "arize_ai/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "- Observe\n- Evaluate\n- Improve\nNew to Arize AX?\nStart here. Instrument your agent, view your first trace, and create your first eval.\nThe Arize AX workflow\n1\nInstrument\nCapture your first trace. Instrumentation adds tracking to your agents to capture traces: step-by-step records of agent activity (inputs, outputs, invoked tools, and costs). After instrumentation, your application streams traces into Arize AX to lay the foundation for measurable improvement.\nUsing a coding agent? Start with Arize Skills. Codex, Cursor, Claude Code, Windsurf, and other coding agents can install the Arize Use the code steps below when you prefer to wire tracing manually or your environment cannot install skills. Learn more about coding-agent setup →\narize-instrumentation skill, inspect your stack, add the right OpenInference setup, and tell you how to verify that traces are flowing.",
    "character_count": 875
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e22b130b-0dff-46e9-9afa-f698d7f117cd",
