    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/bentoml/BentoML",
    "path": "bentoml/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "To report a bug or suggest a feature request, use GitHub Issues.\nThere are many ways to contribute to the project:\n- Report bugs and \"Thumbs up\" on issues that are relevant to you.\n- Investigate issues and review other developers' pull requests.\n- Contribute code or documentation to the project by submitting a GitHub pull request.\n- Check out the Contributing Guide and Development Guide to learn more.\n- Share your feedback and discuss roadmap plans in our forum.\nThanks to all of our amazing contributors!\nThe BentoML framework collects anonymous usage data that helps our community improve the product. Only BentoML's internal API calls are being reported. This excludes any sensitive information, such as user code, model data, model names, or stack traces. Here's the code used for usage tracking. You can opt-out of usage tracking by the --do-not-track CLI option:\nbentoml [command] --do-not-track\nOr by setting the environment variable:\nexport BENTOML_DO_NOT_TRACK=True",
    "character_count": 978
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d8be3f7b-d170-4410-9efe-a22df8b00be3",
    "technology": "BentoML",
    "technology_id": "source-bentoml",
