    "path": "docker_compose/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Docker Compose is a tool for running multi-container applications on Docker\ndefined using the Compose file format.\nA Compose file is used to define how one or more containers that make up\nyour application are configured.\nOnce you have a Compose file, you can create and start your application with a\nsingle command: docker compose up.\nNote: About Docker Swarm Docker Swarm used to rely on the legacy compose file format but did not adopt the compose specification so is missing some of the recent enhancements in the compose syntax. After acquisition by Mirantis swarm isn't maintained by Docker Inc, and as such some Docker Compose features aren't accessible to swarm users.\nDocker Compose is included in Docker Desktop for Windows and macOS.\nYou can download Docker Compose binaries from the release page on this repository.\nRename the relevant binary for your OS to docker-compose and copy it to $HOME/.docker/cli-plugins\nOr copy it into one of these folders to install it system-wide:",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8adfe14c-4a1b-4911-919c-e6dc38040ac3",
    "technology": "Docker Compose",
    "technology_id": "source-docker-compose",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Docker",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
