    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Computer Science > Computation and Language\n[Submitted on 28 May 2020 (v1), last revised 22 Jul 2020 (this version, v4)]\nTitle:Language Models are Few-Shot Learners\nView PDF",
    "character_count": 173
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "7be4400f-d648-49ea-9e47-3fcbf68aa64b",
    "technology": "Few-Shot Prompting",
    "technology_id": "source-few-shot-prompting",
    "category": "prompting",
    "organization": "Independent Research",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "research_papers",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.14165",
    "path": "few_shot_prompting/research_papers.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "Abstract:Recent work has demonstrated substantial gains on many NLP tasks and benchmarks by pre-training on a large corpus of text followed by fine-tuning on a specific task. While typically task-agnostic in architecture, this method still requires task-specific fine-tuning datasets of thousands or tens of thousands of examples. By contrast, humans can generally perform a new language task from only a few examples or from simple instructions - something which current NLP systems still largely struggle to do. Here we show that scaling up language models greatly improves task-agnostic, few-shot performance, sometimes even reaching competitiveness with prior state-of-the-art fine-tuning approaches. Specifically, we train GPT-3, an autoregressive language model with 175 billion parameters, 10x more than any previous non-sparse language model, and test its performance in the few-shot setting",
    "character_count": 899
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f4fb5117-3902-4bda-9210-85fbd9247969",
    "technology": "Few-Shot Prompting",
    "technology_id": "source-few-shot-prompting",
    "category": "prompting",
    "organization": "Independent Research",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "research_papers",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.14165",
    "path": "few_shot_prompting/research_papers.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": ". Specifically, we train GPT-3, an autoregressive language model with 175 billion parameters, 10x more than any previous non-sparse language model, and test its performance in the few-shot setting. For all tasks, GPT-3 is applied without any gradient updates or fine-tuning, with tasks and few-shot demonstrations specified purely via text interaction with the model. GPT-3 achieves strong performance on many NLP datasets, including translation, question-answering, and cloze tasks, as well as several tasks that require on-the-fly reasoning or domain adaptation, such as unscrambling words, using a novel word in a sentence, or performing 3-digit arithmetic. At the same time, we also identify some datasets where GPT-3's few-shot learning still struggles, as well as some datasets where GPT-3 faces methodological issues related to training on large web corpora",
    "character_count": 864
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "14da0b1c-5e49-45f7-a214-11caf6404696",
    "technology": "Few-Shot Prompting",
    "technology_id": "source-few-shot-prompting",
