    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Guidance is an efficient programming paradigm for steering language models. With Guidance, you can control how output is structured and get high-quality output for your use case—while reducing latency and cost vs. conventional prompting or fine-tuning. It allows users to constrain generation (e.g. with regex and CFGs) as well as to interleave control (conditionals, loops, tool use) and generation seamlessly.\nGuidance is available through PyPI and supports a variety of backends (Transformers, llama.cpp, OpenAI, etc.). If you already have the backend required for your model, you can simply run\npip install guidance\nWhen using Guidance, you can work with large language models using common Python idioms:\nfrom guidance import system, user, assistant, gen\nfrom guidance.models import Transformers\n# Could also do LlamaCpp or many other models\nphi_lm = Transformers(\"microsoft/Phi-4-mini-instruct\")\n# Model objects are immutable, so this is a copy\nlm = phi_lm\nwith system():",
