    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Releases: deepset-ai/haystack\nRelease list\nv3.0.0\n⭐️ Highlights\nHaystack 3.0 is a major release for building production-grade agents with full control and flexibility. It ships a wave of new capabilities: a more capable Agent with hooks and first-class skills, built-in run introspection, first-class async for serving, a leaner core, and safer pipeline loading.\nA few small, intentional breaking changes come with it but our Migration Guide and Upgrading to Haystack 3.0 make it easy to upgrade.\n🤖 A more capable, adaptable Agent\nThe Agent gained a general-purpose hooks system and now owns tool execution end to end (the standalone ToolInvoker has been removed). Hooks at before_run, before_llm, before_tool, after_tool, on_exit, and after_run let you shape behavior, enforce guardrails, and add human-in-the-loop checkpoints without touching the agent's internals:\nfrom haystack.components.agents import Agent\nfrom haystack.components.generators.chat import OpenAIChatGenerator",
    "character_count": 980
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e705ee74-e082-4f9b-9a63-5a6dc3474439",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "from haystack.components.agents import Agent\nfrom haystack.components.generators.chat import OpenAIChatGenerator\nfrom haystack.hooks import hook\n@hook\ndef audit_tool_calls(state):\npending = state.data[\"messages\"][-1].tool_calls\nprint(f\"about to run: {[tc.tool_name for tc in pending]}\")\nagent = Agent(\nchat_generator=OpenAIChatGenerator(),\ntools=[...],\nhooks={\"before_tool\": [audit_tool_calls]},\n)\nBuilt on this foundation:\n- Skills as first-class citizens — SkillToolset discovers skills through progressive disclosure, so the model sees only names and one-line descriptions until it loads one, keeping context lean.\n- Dynamic tool selection at runtime — pass tools=... torun /run_async so one reusable Agent serves different teams, tenants, and tasks.\n- Native async tools — @tool routesasync def callables to aTool 's newasync_function .\n- Human-in-the-Loop is now a before_tool hook (ConfirmationHook ).⚠️",
    "character_count": 909
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2bb694e9-4ec4-4802-973d-198bc2e584d3",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "- Native async tools — @tool routesasync def callables to aTool 's newasync_function .\n- Human-in-the-Loop is now a before_tool hook (ConfirmationHook ).⚠️\n- Tool result offloading (ToolResultOffloadHook ) writes large results to a store and leaves a compact pointer in the conversation.\n🔎 Built-in introspection and observability\nAgents now expose step_count, token_usage, and tool_call_counts as built-in state. React to them to compact context when the window fills, cap runaway tool loops, or route to a cheaper approach past a budget threshold. Tracing now emits dedicated step-level spans (haystack.agent.step with nested .llm / .tool children) tagged with the tools actually used, so you can see exactly what your agent did.\n⚡ A core built for serving: first-class async",
    "character_count": 777
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "11362368-8f69-479a-8c14-1d21aadd21b7",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "⚡ A core built for serving: first-class async\nPipeline and AsyncPipeline are now one class — no more switching between them. A single Pipeline exposes run, run_async, run_async_generator, and stream; serialized pipelines, SuperComponents, and PipelineTools load as Pipeline instances.\nfrom haystack import Pipeline\npipeline = Pipeline()\nresult = pipeline.run(data) # synchronous\nresult = await pipeline.run_async(data) # asynchronous\nConcurrent tool calls and token-by-token streaming come standard: Pipeline.stream() yields StreamingChunks as they're produced and exposes the final output on handle.result — the lower latency and streaming UX serving apps need. Components and Pipeline also get a symmetric lifecycle — warm_up to acquire, close to release — so long-running services don't leak connections, GPU memory, or file handles. External resources (and API keys) are now created at warm_up, not in __init__.\n🧱 A leaner, faster-moving framework ⚠️",
    "character_count": 954
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "4ec13732-1efa-440e-bcbe-088b58975fb2",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "🧱 A leaner, faster-moving framework ⚠️\nLegacy Generators are gone, haystack-experimental is no longer a core dependency, and 30 components now live in independently released packages in haystack-core-integrations: Sentence Transformers, local & API Hugging Face, Whisper, spaCy/langdetect, Tika and Azure OCR, SerperDev/SearchApi, OpenAPI connectors, and the Datadog/OpenTelemetry tracers. As a result, there are fewer transitive dependencies to audit and we can ship independent of the core release cycle. Migration is an install plus an import change:\n# pip install sentence-transformers-haystack\n# Before: from haystack.components.embedders import SentenceTransformersTextEmbedder\nfrom haystack_integrations.components.embedders.sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformersTextEmbedder\nThe full old → new import table is in MIGRATION.md.\n💬 Chat Generators everywhere (legacy Generators removed) ⚠️",
    "character_count": 905
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a06aafaa-902a-452e-93af-24496782ef47",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "The full old → new import table is in MIGRATION.md.\n💬 Chat Generators everywhere (legacy Generators removed) ⚠️\nOpenAIGenerator, AzureOpenAIGenerator, HuggingFaceAPIGenerator, and HuggingFaceLocalGenerator have been removed in favor of their Chat Generator counterparts. To ease the switch, all Chat Generators now accept a plain str for messages:\n# Before\nfrom haystack.components.generators import OpenAIGenerator\ntext = OpenAIGenerator().run(\"What is NLP?\")[\"replies\"][0] # str\n# After\nfrom haystack.components.generators.chat import OpenAIChatGenerator\nreply = OpenAIChatGenerator().run(\"What is NLP?\")[\"replies\"][0] # ChatMessage\ntext = reply.text # str; metadata in reply.meta\nDALLEImageGenerator was also renamed to OpenAIImageGenerator.\n🔒 Safer pipeline loading ⚠️",
    "character_count": 772
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f8a57bec-43c0-42aa-b448-66949c152970",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "text = reply.text # str; metadata in reply.meta\nDALLEImageGenerator was also renamed to OpenAIImageGenerator.\n🔒 Safer pipeline loading ⚠️\nPipeline deserialization (Pipeline.load / loads / from_dict) is now gated by a trusted-module allowlist (haystack, haystack_integrations, haystack_experimental, builtins, typing, collections by default), and dangerous builtins like eval, exec, open, and getattr can no longer be resolved. Allowlist custom modules when needed:\nPipeline.load(fp, allowed_modules=[\"mypkg.*\"]) # or HAYSTACK_DESERIALIZATION_ALLOWLIST / allow_deserialization_module(...)\nPipeline.load(fp, unsafe=True) # only if you fully trust the source\n🧪 Testing without the API bill\nNewly added mock components mean no API keys, no network, no flaky CI for testing and prototyping. MockChatGenerator returns predefined responses, MockTextEmbedder and MockDocumentEmbedder return stable, hash-derived embeddings.\nA few smaller breaking changes to know about",
    "character_count": 960
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "cb0678a6-8721-40bb-a4c9-975284d60fd0",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "A few smaller breaking changes to know about\n- Required template variables by default — Agent ,PromptBuilder , andChatPromptBuilder now treat every Jinja2 variable as required (required_variables=None restores the old behavior); a new{% insert %} tag interleaves runtime messages.⚠️\n- No more implicit State injection by name — tools must declareinputs_from_state explicitly to read aState value; same-named parameters no longer fill in automatically.⚠️\n- Deterministic Document.id — computed from canonical, key-sorted JSON ofmeta , so documents with non-emptymeta get different IDs than in 2.x.⚠️\n- Scoped logging — configure_logging attaches to Haystack's own loggers; importing Haystack no longer reconfiguresstructlog process-wide.⚠️\n- Explicit tracing — no longer auto-enabled; add an OpenTelemetryConnector /DatadogConnector or calltracing.enable_tracing(...) .⚠️\nSee the Upgrade Notes below for the full list.\n⬆️ Upgrade Notes\n-",
    "character_count": 936
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "33e2e229-8cae-4952-8bb8-34650ca4220d",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "AsyncPipeline has been removed. Its asynchronous capabilities are now part of the singlePipeline class, which provides both a synchronousrun method and the asynchronousrun_async ,run_async_generator , andstream methods (mirroring how components exposerun andrun_async ).To migrate, replace AsyncPipeline withPipeline :# Before from haystack import AsyncPipeline pipeline = AsyncPipeline() result = await pipeline.run_async(data) # After from haystack import Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline() result = await pipeline.run_async(data) Serialized pipelines, SuperComponent s, andPipelineTool s are loaded asPipeline instances.Pipeline.run runs synchronously and blocks until completion; in an async context useawait pipeline.run_async(...) . The formerAsyncPipeline.run was a synchronous wrapper around the concurrent engine, so to preserve that behavior useasyncio.run(pipeline.run_async(...))",
    "character_count": 887
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c13f3e7d-9d5d-466e-a577-aeaa7431ce43",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": ". The formerAsyncPipeline.run was a synchronous wrapper around the concurrent engine, so to preserve that behavior useasyncio.run(pipeline.run_async(...)) . Note thatPipeline.run executes components sequentially and does not acceptconcurrency_limit .Both synchronous and asynchronous runs are traced under a single haystack.pipeline.run operation name, distinguished by ahaystack.pipeline.execution_mode tag (sync orasync ). Previously, asynchronous runs used thehaystack.async_pipeline.run operation name.",
    "character_count": 506
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "046879c5-05bc-42ad-8bb7-b07079db3d04",
    "technology": "Haystack",
    "technology_id": "source-haystack",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "deepset",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/releases",
    "path": "haystack/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "-\ncontinue_run is now a reserved key inAgent.state_schema (set by anon_exit hook to keep the Agent running). Passing it via thestate_schema argument now raisesValueError . Rename any conflicting state key (e.g.my_continue_run ) to migrate.\n-\nAgent no longer validatesexit_conditions against tool names at initialization. Exit conditions are now evaluated at runtime, so a condition naming a tool that is loaded later — e.g. a tool passed at runtime or one discovered bySearchableToolset — works as expected. Consequently, an unknown exit-condition name no longer raises aValueError at construction.\n-\nTool support is now validated against the tools resolved for each run, not only the tools provided at initialization. Passing tools at runtime via run(tools=...) to a chat generator that does not support tools now raises aTypeError instead of silently ignoring them.\n-",
    "character_count": 869
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "610fd850-ea0e-4b81-8c27-ed250cdc8619",
