    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "{\n\"role\": \"system\",\n\"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant.\"\n},\n{\n\"role\": \"user\",\n\"content\": \"What is deep learning?\"\n}\n],\n\"stream\": true,\n\"max_tokens\": 20\n}' \\\n-H 'Content-Type: application/json'\nNote: To use NVIDIA GPUs, you need to install the NVIDIA Container Toolkit. We also recommend using NVIDIA drivers with CUDA version 12.2 or higher. For running the Docker container on a machine with no GPUs or CUDA support, it is enough to remove the --gpus all flag and add --disable-custom-kernels, please note CPU is not the intended platform for this project, so performance might be subpar.\nNote: TGI supports AMD Instinct MI210 and MI250 GPUs. Details can be found in the Supported Hardware documentation. To use AMD GPUs, please use docker run --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --shm-size 1g -p 8080:80 -v $volume:/data ghcr.io/huggingface/text-generation-inference:3.3.5-rocm --model-id $model instead of the command above.",
    "character_count": 932
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fe3d7c7a-1d04-4653-8bbe-c2cbe922f637",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "To see all options to serve your models (in the code or in the cli):\ntext-generation-launcher --help\nYou can consult the OpenAPI documentation of the text-generation-inference REST API using the /docs route.\nThe Swagger UI is also available at: https://huggingface.github.io/text-generation-inference.\nYou have the option to utilize the HF_TOKEN environment variable for configuring the token employed by\ntext-generation-inference. This allows you to gain access to protected resources.\nFor example, if you want to serve the gated Llama V2 model variants:\n- Go to https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens\n- Copy your CLI READ token\n- Export HF_TOKEN=<your CLI READ token>\nor with Docker:\nmodel=meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct\nvolume=$PWD/data # share a volume with the Docker container to avoid downloading weights every run\ntoken=<your cli READ token>\ndocker run --gpus all --shm-size 1g -e HF_TOKEN=$token -p 8080:80 -v $volume:/data \\",
    "character_count": 941
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "75d42853-fba4-40f1-bec0-b2c8004aa89e",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "token=<your cli READ token>\ndocker run --gpus all --shm-size 1g -e HF_TOKEN=$token -p 8080:80 -v $volume:/data \\\nghcr.io/huggingface/text-generation-inference:3.3.5 --model-id $model\nNCCL is a communication framework used by\nPyTorch to do distributed training/inference. text-generation-inference makes\nuse of NCCL to enable Tensor Parallelism to dramatically speed up inference for large language models.\nIn order to share data between the different devices of a NCCL group, NCCL might fall back to using the host memory if\npeer-to-peer using NVLink or PCI is not possible.\nTo allow the container to use 1G of Shared Memory and support SHM sharing, we add --shm-size 1g on the above command.\nIf you are running text-generation-inference inside Kubernetes. You can also add Shared Memory to the container by\ncreating a volume with:\n- name: shm\nemptyDir:\nmedium: Memory\nsizeLimit: 1Gi\nand mounting it to /dev/shm.",
    "character_count": 912
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "9bd759ee-e156-4661-a487-b9697c9fb52f",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "creating a volume with:\n- name: shm\nemptyDir:\nmedium: Memory\nsizeLimit: 1Gi\nand mounting it to /dev/shm.\nFinally, you can also disable SHM sharing by using the NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=1 environment variable. However, note that\nthis will impact performance.\ntext-generation-inference is instrumented with distributed tracing using OpenTelemetry. You can use this feature\nby setting the address to an OTLP collector with the --otlp-endpoint argument. The default service name can be\noverridden with the --otlp-service-name argument\nDetailed blogpost by Adyen on TGI inner workings: LLM inference at scale with TGI (Martin Iglesias Goyanes - Adyen, 2024)\nYou can also opt to install text-generation-inference locally.\nFirst clone the repository and change directory into it:\ngit clone https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference\ncd text-generation-inference\nThen install Rust and create a Python virtual environment with at least\nPython 3.9, e.g. using conda or python venv:",
    "character_count": 977
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "85726751-c708-4621-b22c-1ad1aa381e81",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "cd text-generation-inference\nThen install Rust and create a Python virtual environment with at least\nPython 3.9, e.g. using conda or python venv:\ncurl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n#using conda\nconda create -n text-generation-inference python=3.11\nconda activate text-generation-inference\n#using python venv\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\nYou may also need to install Protoc.\nOn Linux:\nPROTOC_ZIP=protoc-21.12-linux-x86_64.zip\ncurl -OL https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/releases/download/v21.12/$PROTOC_ZIP\nsudo unzip -o $PROTOC_ZIP -d /usr/local bin/protoc\nsudo unzip -o $PROTOC_ZIP -d /usr/local 'include/*'\nrm -f $PROTOC_ZIP\nOn MacOS, using Homebrew:\nbrew install protobuf\nThen run:\nBUILD_EXTENSIONS=True make install # Install repository and HF/transformer fork with CUDA kernels\ntext-generation-launcher --model-id mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2",
    "character_count": 909
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c01e5af9-e9e7-442b-aeba-8f63a5eb9ccb",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": "Then run:\nBUILD_EXTENSIONS=True make install # Install repository and HF/transformer fork with CUDA kernels\ntext-generation-launcher --model-id mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2\nNote: on some machines, you may also need the OpenSSL libraries and gcc. On Linux machines, run:\nsudo apt-get install libssl-dev gcc -y\nAnother option is to install text-generation-inference locally using Nix. Currently,\nwe only support Nix on x86_64 Linux with CUDA GPUs. When using Nix, all dependencies can\nbe pulled from a binary cache, removing the need to build them locally.\nFirst follow the instructions to install Cachix and enable the Hugging Face cache. Setting up the cache is important, otherwise Nix will build many of the dependencies locally, which can take hours.\nAfter that you can run TGI with nix run:\ncd text-generation-inference\nnix run --extra-experimental-features nix-command --extra-experimental-features flakes . -- --model-id meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct",
    "character_count": 965
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "334175aa-af92-426f-97e7-5fd591f1fd37",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "cd text-generation-inference\nnix run --extra-experimental-features nix-command --extra-experimental-features flakes . -- --model-id meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct\nNote: when you are using Nix on a non-NixOS system, you have to make some symlinks to make the CUDA driver libraries visible to Nix packages.\nFor TGI development, you can use the impure dev shell:\nnix develop .#impure\n# Only needed the first time the devshell is started or after updating the protobuf.\n(\ncd server\nmkdir text_generation_server/pb || true\npython -m grpc_tools.protoc -I../proto/v3 --python_out=text_generation_server/pb \\\n--grpc_python_out=text_generation_server/pb --mypy_out=text_generation_server/pb ../proto/v3/generate.proto\nfind text_generation_server/pb/ -type f -name \"*.py\" -print0 -exec sed -i -e 's/^\\(import.*pb2\\)/from . \\1/g' {} \\;\ntouch text_generation_server/pb/__init__.py\n)\nAll development dependencies (cargo, Python, Torch), etc. are available in this dev shell.",
    "character_count": 963
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "09eb9c66-bb39-4264-a7e4-0d1b4e8e2e19",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
    "technology_id": "source-hf-tgi",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/text-generation-inference",
    "path": "hugging_face_text_generation_inference_tgi/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "text": "touch text_generation_server/pb/__init__.py\n)\nAll development dependencies (cargo, Python, Torch), etc. are available in this dev shell.\nTGI works out of the box to serve optimized models for all modern models. They can be found in this list.\nOther architectures are supported on a best-effort basis using:\nAutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(<model>, device_map=\"auto\")\nor\nAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(<model>, device_map=\"auto\")\ntext-generation-launcher --model-id mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2\nYou can also run pre-quantized weights (AWQ, GPTQ, Marlin) or on-the-fly quantize weights with bitsandbytes, EETQ, fp8, to reduce the VRAM requirement:\ntext-generation-launcher --model-id mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2 --quantize\n4bit quantization is available using the NF4 and FP4 data types from bitsandbytes. It can be enabled by providing --quantize bitsandbytes-nf4 or --quantize bitsandbytes-fp4 as a command line argument to text-generation-launcher.",
    "character_count": 974
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "1d8c7f15-1fd7-4536-9db2-fa307b9b1e40",
    "technology": "Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI)",
