    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/k3s-io/k3s",
    "path": "k3s/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": "# On a different node run the below. NODE_TOKEN comes from\n# /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/node-token on your server\nsudo k3s agent --server https://myserver:6443 --token ${NODE_TOKEN}\nPlease check out our contributing guide if you're interested in contributing to K3s.\nSecurity issues in K3s can be reported by sending an email to security@k3s.io. Please do not file issues about security issues.",
    "character_count": 395
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "44131ad4-2255-489a-9ff7-7586cceb3790",
    "technology": "K3s",
    "technology_id": "source-k3s",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Rancher",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.k3s.io/",
    "path": "k3s/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Lightweight Kubernetes. Easy to install, half the memory, all in a binary of less than 100 MB.\nGreat for:\n- Edge\n- Homelab\n- Internet of Things (IoT)\n- Continuous Integration (CI)\n- Development\n- Single board computers (ARM)\n- Air-gapped environments\n- Embedded K8s\n- Situations where a PhD in K8s clusterology is infeasible\nWhat is K3s?\nK3s is a fully compliant Kubernetes distribution with the following enhancements:\n- Distributed as a single binary or minimal container image.\n- Lightweight datastore based on sqlite3 as the default storage backend. etcd3, MySQL, and Postgres are also available.\n- Wrapped in simple launcher that handles a lot of the complexity of TLS and options.\n- Secure by default with reasonable defaults for lightweight environments.\n- Operation of all Kubernetes control plane components is encapsulated in a single binary and process, allowing K3s to automate and manage complex cluster operations like distributing certificates.",
    "character_count": 959
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b770b8b8-c758-4998-af03-7026f3698772",
    "technology": "K3s",
    "technology_id": "source-k3s",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Rancher",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.k3s.io/",
    "path": "k3s/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "- Operation of all Kubernetes control plane components is encapsulated in a single binary and process, allowing K3s to automate and manage complex cluster operations like distributing certificates.\n- External dependencies have been minimized; the only requirements are a modern kernel and cgroup mounts.\n- Packages the required dependencies for easy \"batteries-included\" cluster creation:\n- containerd / cri-dockerd container runtime (CRI)\n- Flannel Container Network Interface (CNI)\n- CoreDNS Cluster DNS\n- Traefik Ingress controller\n- ServiceLB Load-Balancer controller\n- Kube-router Network Policy controller\n- Local-path-provisioner Persistent Volume controller\n- Spegel distributed container image registry mirror\n- Host utilities (iptables, socat, etc)\nWhat's with the name?",
    "character_count": 780
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8dfa372f-3f6f-4b45-9cd8-7cee03df4949",
    "technology": "K3s",
    "technology_id": "source-k3s",
    "category": "deployment",
    "organization": "Rancher",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.k3s.io/",
    "path": "k3s/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "- Local-path-provisioner Persistent Volume controller\n- Spegel distributed container image registry mirror\n- Host utilities (iptables, socat, etc)\nWhat's with the name?\nWe wanted an installation of Kubernetes that was half the size in terms of memory footprint. Kubernetes is a 10-letter word stylized as K8s. So something half as big as Kubernetes would be a 5-letter word stylized as K3s. There is no long form of K3s and no official pronunciation.",
    "character_count": 450
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b13f53e2-12bc-4fdb-aff1-2af09350b0a1",
    "technology": "KServe",
    "technology_id": "source-kserve",
