    "path": "llama_factory/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "text": "Additional dependencies for specific features are available in examples/requirements/.\ndocker run -it --rm --gpus=all --ipc=host hiyouga/llamafactory:latest\nThis image is built on Ubuntu 22.04 (x86_64), CUDA 12.4, Python 3.11, PyTorch 2.6.0, and Flash-attn 2.7.4.\nFind the pre-built images: https://hub.docker.com/r/hiyouga/llamafactory/tags\nPlease refer to build docker to build the image yourself.\nSetting up a virtual environment with uv\nCreate an isolated Python environment with uv:\nuv run llamafactory-cli webui\nFor Windows users\nYou need to manually install the GPU version of PyTorch on the Windows platform. Please refer to the official website and the following command to install PyTorch with CUDA support:\npip uninstall torch torchvision torchaudio\npip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126\npython -c \"import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())\"\nIf you see True then you have successfully installed PyTorch with CUDA support.",
    "character_count": 991
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "13ace7cb-7e63-456f-9481-a13287dabcae",
    "technology": "LLaMA-Factory",
    "technology_id": "source-llama-factory",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "hiyouga",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "llama_factory/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "text": "python -c \"import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())\"\nIf you see True then you have successfully installed PyTorch with CUDA support.\nTry dataloader_num_workers: 0 if you encounter Can't pickle local object error.\nTo enable Quantized LoRA (QLoRA) on Windows, you need to install bitsandbytes.\nFor most users, it is recommended to install the latest official release:\npip install bitsandbytes\nIf you are using uv to manage your virtual environment, it is recommended to install bitsandbytes after installing the GPU-enabled version of PyTorch:\nuv pip install bitsandbytes --no-deps\n[!IMPORTANT] Pay attention to the CUDA Toolkit version when installing bitsandbytes. Official bitsandbytes releases are built for specific CUDA Toolkit versions. On Windows x86-64, separate builds are currently provided for CUDA 11.8–12.6 and CUDA 12.8–12.9. Support for NVIDIA RTX 50 Series GPUs (e.g., RTX 5060 Ti, sm_120) requires the CUDA 12.8–12.9 builds.",
    "character_count": 946
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "5b28a312-1ad5-4f34-a629-8753ee6c6b3f",
    "technology": "LLaMA-Factory",
    "technology_id": "source-llama-factory",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "hiyouga",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "llama_factory/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "text": "If your environment uses an older CUDA version, or you need compatibility with older Windows / PyTorch combinations, you can install the third-party precompiled Windows wheel:\npip install https://github.com/jllllll/bitsandbytes-windows-webui/releases/download/wheels/bitsandbytes-0.41.2.post2-py3-none-win_amd64.whl\nTo enable FlashAttention-2 on the Windows platform, please use the script from flash-attention-windows-wheel to compile and install it by yourself.\nFor Ascend NPU users\nTo install LLaMA Factory on Ascend NPU devices, please upgrade Python to version 3.10 or higher: pip install -r requirements/npu.txt. Additionally, you need to install the Ascend CANN Toolkit and Kernels. Please follow the installation tutorial.\nYou can also download the pre-built Docker images:\n# Docker Hub\ndocker pull hiyouga/llamafactory:latest-cann9.0.0-torch_npu2.7.1-A2-ubuntu-py3.11\ndocker pull hiyouga/llamafactory:latest-cann9.0.0-torch_npu2.7.1-A3-ubuntu-py3.11",
    "character_count": 958
  },
