    "path": "lmql/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "This launches a browser-based playground IDE, including a showcase of many exemplary LMQL programs. If the IDE does not launch automatically, go to http://localhost:3000.\nAlternatively, lmql run can be used to execute local .lmql files. Note that when using local HuggingFace Transformers models in the Playground IDE or via lmql run, you have to first launch an instance of the LMQL Inference API for the corresponding model via the command lmql serve-model.\nIf you want to use OpenAI models, you have to configure your API credentials. To do so you can either define the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable or create a file api.env in the active working directory, with the following contents:\nopenai-org: <org identifier>\nopenai-secret: <api secret>\nFor system-wide configuration, you can also create an api.env file at $HOME/.lmql/api.env or at the project root of your LMQL distribution (e.g. src/ in a development copy).",
    "character_count": 926
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "4b3cd40e-f0c4-47ac-9488-558fee238a55",
    "technology": "LMQL",
    "technology_id": "source-lmql",
    "category": "prompting",
    "organization": "ETH Zurich",
    "license": "MIT",
