    "url": "https://github.com/eth-sri/lmql/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "lmql/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "For system-wide configuration, you can also create an api.env file at $HOME/.lmql/api.env or at the project root of your LMQL distribution (e.g. src/ in a development copy).\nAlternatively, you can use LMQL-specific env variables LMQL_OPENAI_SECRET and LMQL_OPENAI_ORG.\nTo install the latest (bleeding-edge) version of LMQL, you can also run the following command:\npip install git+https://github.com/eth-sri/lmql\nThis will install the lmql package directly from the main branch of this repository. We do not continously test the main version, so it may be less stable than the latest PyPI release.\nLMQL is a community-centric project. If you are interested in contributing to LMQL, please see the contributing guidelines for more information, and reach out to us via Discord. We are looking forward to your contributions!\nTo setup a conda environment for local LMQL development with GPU support, run the following commands:\n# prepare conda environment",
    "character_count": 950
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d859baa5-29a9-400c-9ad1-ae492c985a35",
    "technology": "LMQL",
    "technology_id": "source-lmql",
    "category": "prompting",
    "organization": "ETH Zurich",
    "license": "MIT",
