    "path": "litgpt/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "text": "📊 SAMBA: Simple Hybrid State Space Models for Efficient Unlimited Context Language Modeling\nThe Samba project by researchers at Microsoft is built on top of the LitGPT code base and combines state space models with sliding window attention, which outperforms pure state space models.\n🏆 NeurIPS 2023 Large Language Model Efficiency Challenge: 1 LLM + 1 GPU + 1 Day\nThe LitGPT repository was the official starter kit for the NeurIPS 2023 LLM Efficiency Challenge, which is a competition focused on finetuning an existing non-instruction tuned LLM for 24 hours on a single GPU.\n🦙 TinyLlama: An Open-Source Small Language Model\nLitGPT powered the TinyLlama project and TinyLlama: An Open-Source Small Language Model research paper.\n🍪 MicroLlama: MicroLlama-300M\nMicroLlama is a 300M Llama model pretrained on 50B tokens powered by TinyLlama and LitGPT.\n🔬 Pre-training Small Base LMs with Fewer Tokens",
    "character_count": 896
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2b12e129-758c-49cd-baab-599cbf5615c0",
    "technology": "LitGPT",
    "technology_id": "source-litgpt",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Lightning AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/Lightning-AI/litgpt/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "litgpt/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "text": "🍪 MicroLlama: MicroLlama-300M\nMicroLlama is a 300M Llama model pretrained on 50B tokens powered by TinyLlama and LitGPT.\n🔬 Pre-training Small Base LMs with Fewer Tokens\nThe research paper \"Pre-training Small Base LMs with Fewer Tokens\", which utilizes LitGPT, develops smaller base language models by inheriting a few transformer blocks from larger models and training on a tiny fraction of the data used by the larger models. It demonstrates that these smaller models can perform comparably to larger models despite using significantly less training data and resources.\nWe welcome all individual contributors, regardless of their level of experience or hardware. Your contributions are valuable, and we are excited to see what you can accomplish in this collaborative and supportive environment.\n🚀 Get started\n⚡️ Finetuning, incl. LoRA, QLoRA, and Adapters\n🤖 Pretraining\n💬 Model evaluation\n📘 Supported and custom datasets\n🧹 Quantization\n🤯 Tips for dealing with out-of-memory (OOM) errors",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e5a610d2-5920-431d-8f16-68ff3a1bc65f",
    "technology": "LitGPT",
    "technology_id": "source-litgpt",
