    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "# rebuild storage context\nstorage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=\"./storage\")\n# load index\nindex = load_index_from_storage(storage_context)\nBy default, llama-index-core includes a _static folder that contains the nltk and tiktoken cache that is included with the package installation. This ensures that you can easily run llama-index in environments with restrictive disk access permissions at runtime.\nTo verify that these files are safe and valid, we use the github attest-build-provenance action. This action will verify that the files in the _static folder are the same as the files in the llama-index-core/llama_index/core/_static folder.\nTo verify this, you can run the following script (pointing to your installed package):\n#!/bin/bash\nSTATIC_DIR=\"venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/llama_index/core/_static\"\nREPO=\"run-llama/llama_index\"\nfind \"$STATIC_DIR\" -type f | while read -r file; do\necho \"Verifying: $file\"",
    "character_count": 939
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ac5a19e9-5192-4702-8a83-e785fa8e7f8d",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/run-llama/llama_index",
    "path": "llamaindex/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "#!/bin/bash\nSTATIC_DIR=\"venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/llama_index/core/_static\"\nREPO=\"run-llama/llama_index\"\nfind \"$STATIC_DIR\" -type f | while read -r file; do\necho \"Verifying: $file\"\ngh attestation verify \"$file\" -R \"$REPO\" || echo \"Failed to verify: $file\"\ndone\nReference to cite if you use LlamaIndex in a paper:\n@software{Liu_LlamaIndex_2022,\nauthor = {Liu, Jerry},\ndoi = {10.5281/zenodo.1234},\nmonth = {11},\ntitle = {{LlamaIndex}},\nurl = {https://github.com/jerryjliu/llama_index},\nyear = {2022}\n}",
    "character_count": 507
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8bdf03aa-077b-4245-8149-8e94a269f9f0",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Welcome to LlamaIndex 🦙 !\nLlamaIndex is the leading framework for building LLM-powered agents over your data with LLMs and workflows.\n-\nIntroduction What is context augmentation? What are agents and workflows? How does LlamaIndex help build them?\n-\nUse cases What kind of apps can you build with LlamaIndex? Who should use it?\n-\nGetting started Get started in Python or TypeScript in just 5 lines of code!\n-\nLlamaCloud Managed services for LlamaIndex including LlamaParse, the world’s best document parser.\n-\nCommunity Get help and meet collaborators on Discord, Twitter, LinkedIn, and learn how to contribute to the project.\n-\nRelated projects Check out our library of connectors, readers, and other integrations at LlamaHub as well as demos and starter apps like create-llama.\nIntroduction\nSection titled “Introduction”\nWhat are agents?\nSection titled “What are agents?”",
    "character_count": 872
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d4f87a9e-9126-4053-abd8-bcba8d27621b",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "Introduction\nSection titled “Introduction”\nWhat are agents?\nSection titled “What are agents?”\nAgents are LLM-powered knowledge assistants that use tools to perform tasks like research, data extraction, and more. Agents range from simple question-answering to being able to sense, decide and take actions in order to complete tasks.\nLlamaIndex provides a framework for building agents including the ability to use RAG pipelines as one of many tools to complete a task.\nWhat are workflows?\nSection titled “What are workflows?”\nWorkflows are multi-step processes that combine one or more agents, data connectors, and other tools to complete a task. They are event-driven software that allows you to combine RAG data sources and multiple agents to create a complex application that can perform a wide variety of tasks with reflection, error-correction, and other hallmarks of advanced LLM applications. You can then deploy these agentic workflows as production microservices.",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "1411d42f-d413-4e6d-b525-94ab94985188",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "What is context augmentation?\nSection titled “What is context augmentation?”\nLLMs offer a natural language interface between humans and data. LLMs come pre-trained on huge amounts of publicly available data, but they are not trained on your data. Your data may be private or specific to the problem you’re trying to solve. It’s behind APIs, in SQL databases, or trapped in PDFs and slide decks.\nContext augmentation makes your data available to the LLM to solve the problem at hand. LlamaIndex provides the tools to build any of context-augmentation use case, from prototype to production. Our tools allow you to ingest, parse, index and process your data and quickly implement complex query workflows combining data access with LLM prompting.\nThe most popular example of context-augmentation is Retrieval-Augmented Generation or RAG, which combines context with LLMs at inference time.\nLlamaIndex is the framework for Context-Augmented LLM Applications",
    "character_count": 953
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "7ee661ef-d4e7-4434-96cf-40119710054a",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "LlamaIndex is the framework for Context-Augmented LLM Applications\nSection titled “LlamaIndex is the framework for Context-Augmented LLM Applications”\nLlamaIndex imposes no restriction on how you use LLMs. You can use LLMs as auto-complete, chatbots, agents, and more. It just makes using them easier. We provide tools like:\n- Data connectors ingest your existing data from their native source and format. These could be APIs, PDFs, SQL, and (much) more.\n- Data indexes structure your data in intermediate representations that are easy and performant for LLMs to consume.\n- Engines provide natural language access to your data. For example:\n- Query engines are powerful interfaces for question-answering (e.g. a RAG flow).\n- Chat engines are conversational interfaces for multi-message, “back and forth” interactions with your data.\n- Agents are LLM-powered knowledge workers augmented by tools, from simple helper functions to API integrations and more.",
    "character_count": 954
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "9da8bf84-118a-4d94-9713-6944fc7e899d",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "- Agents are LLM-powered knowledge workers augmented by tools, from simple helper functions to API integrations and more.\n- Observability/Evaluation integrations that enable you to rigorously experiment, evaluate, and monitor your app in a virtuous cycle.\n- Workflows allow you to combine all of the above into an event-driven system far more flexible than other, graph-based approaches.\nUse cases\nSection titled “Use cases”\nSome popular use cases for LlamaIndex and context augmentation in general include:\n- Question-Answering (Retrieval-Augmented Generation aka RAG)\n- Chatbots\n- Document Understanding and Data Extraction\n- Autonomous Agents that can perform research and take actions\n- Multi-modal applications that combine text, images, and other data types\n- Fine-tuning models on data to improve performance\nCheck out our use cases documentation for more examples and links to tutorials.\n👨👩👧👦 Who is LlamaIndex for?\nSection titled “👨👩👧👦 Who is LlamaIndex for?”",
    "character_count": 968
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "4592842a-0f4d-42dc-9d0f-fa4db094d0d0",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "Check out our use cases documentation for more examples and links to tutorials.\n👨👩👧👦 Who is LlamaIndex for?\nSection titled “👨👩👧👦 Who is LlamaIndex for?”\nLlamaIndex provides tools for beginners, advanced users, and everyone in between.\nOur high-level API allows beginner users to use LlamaIndex to ingest and query their data in 5 lines of code.\nFor more complex applications, our lower-level APIs allow advanced users to customize and extend any module — data connectors, indices, retrievers, query engines, and reranking modules — to fit their needs.\nGetting Started\nSection titled “Getting Started”\nLlamaIndex is available in Python (these docs) and Typescript. If you’re not sure where to start, we recommend reading how to read these docs which will point you to the right place based on your experience level.\n30 second quickstart\nSection titled “30 second quickstart”\nSet an environment variable called OPENAI_API_KEY with an OpenAI API key. Install the Python library:",
    "character_count": 975
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c7b397be-95e7-4b5d-8ca9-8ef9ea59ecbf",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
