    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "30 second quickstart\nSection titled “30 second quickstart”\nSet an environment variable called OPENAI_API_KEY with an OpenAI API key. Install the Python library:\nPut some documents in a folder called data, then ask questions about them with our famous 5-line starter:\nIf any part of this trips you up, don’t worry! Check out our more comprehensive starter tutorials using remote APIs like OpenAI or any model that runs on your laptop.\nLlamaCloud\nSection titled “LlamaCloud”\nIf you’re an enterprise developer, check out LlamaCloud. It is an end-to-end managed service for document parsing, extraction, indexing, and retrieval - allowing you to get production-quality data for your AI agent. You can sign up and get 10,000 free credits per month, sign up for one of our plans, or come talk to us if you’re interested in an enterprise solution. We offer both SaaS and self-hosted plans.\nYou can also check out the LlamaCloud documentation for more details.",
    "character_count": 952
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "73f71520-7f86-45ba-a869-f4d07c312e07",
    "technology": "LlamaIndex",
    "technology_id": "source-llamaindex",
    "category": "frameworks",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://docs.llamaindex.ai/",
    "path": "llamaindex/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "You can also check out the LlamaCloud documentation for more details.\n- Document Parsing (LlamaParse): LlamaParse is the best-in-class document parsing solution. It’s powered by VLMs and perfect for even the most complex documents (nested tables, embedded charts/images, and more). Learn more or check out the docs.\n- Document Extraction (LlamaExtract): Given a human-defined or inferred schema, extract structured data from any document. Learn more or check out the docs.\n- Indexing/Retrieval: Set up an e2e pipeline to index a collection of documents for retrieval. Connect your data source (e.g. Sharepoint, Google Drive, S3), your vector DB data sink, and we automatically handle the document processing and syncing. Learn more or check out the docs.\nCommunity\nSection titled “Community”\nNeed help? Have a feature suggestion? Join the LlamaIndex community:\nGetting the library\nSection titled “Getting the library”\n- LlamaIndex Python\n- LlamaIndex Python Github",
    "character_count": 964
  },
  {
