    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models/blob/main/models/llama3_1/MODEL_CARD.md",
    "path": "meta_llama/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "The Meta Llama 3.1 collection of multilingual large language models (LLMs) is a collection of pretrained and instruction tuned generative models in 8B, 70B and 405B sizes (text in/text out). The Llama 3.1 instruction tuned text only models (8B, 70B, 405B) are optimized for multilingual dialogue use cases and outperform many of the available open source and closed chat models on common industry benchmarks.\nModel developer: Meta\nModel Architecture: Llama 3.1 is an auto-regressive language model that uses an optimized transformer architecture. The tuned versions use supervised fine-tuning (SFT) and reinforcement learning with human feedback (RLHF) to align with human preferences for helpfulness and safety.\n| | Training Data | Params | Input modalities | Output modalities | Context length | GQA | Token count | Knowledge cutoff |\n| Llama 3.1 (text only) | A new mix of publicly available online data. | 8B | Multilingual Text | Multilingual Text and code | 128k | Yes | 15T+ | December 2023 |",
    "character_count": 999
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f2baff9e-eceb-47ed-ad9e-76c0a26cdcc1",
    "technology": "Meta Llama",
    "technology_id": "source-meta-llama",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Meta",
    "license": "Llama 3 Community License",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models/blob/main/models/llama3_1/MODEL_CARD.md",
    "path": "meta_llama/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "| Llama 3.1 (text only) | A new mix of publicly available online data. | 8B | Multilingual Text | Multilingual Text and code | 128k | Yes | 15T+ | December 2023 |\n| | | 70B | Multilingual Text | Multilingual Text and code | 128k | Yes | | |\n| | | 405B | Multilingual Text | Multilingual Text and code | 128k | Yes | | |\nSupported languages: English, German, French, Italian, Portuguese, Hindi, Spanish, and Thai.\nLlama 3.1 family of models. Token counts refer to pretraining data only. All model versions use Grouped-Query Attention (GQA) for improved inference scalability.\nModel Release Date: July 23, 2024.\nStatus: This is a static model trained on an offline dataset. Future versions of the tuned models will be released as we improve model safety with community feedback.\nLicense: A custom commercial license, the Llama 3.1 Community License, is available at: https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models/blob/main/models/llama3_1/LICENSE",
    "character_count": 941
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "886bf4b6-f7c3-47b2-a0da-8f94b75db8e6",
    "technology": "Meta Llama",
    "technology_id": "source-meta-llama",
