    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models",
    "path": "meta_llama/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "llama-model list # List available models\nllama-model list --show-all # List all models (including older versions)\nllama-model describe -m MODEL_ID # Show detailed information about a model\nllama-model download # Download models from Meta or Hugging Face\nllama-model verify-download # Verify integrity of downloaded models\nllama-model remove -m MODEL_ID # Remove a downloaded model\nllama-model prompt-format -m MODEL_ID # Show the prompt format for a model\nFor detailed help on any command, run llama-model COMMAND --help.\nIn order to run the models, you will need to install dependencies after checking out the repository.\n# Run this within a suitable Python environment (uv, conda, or virtualenv)\npip install .[torch]\nExample scripts are available in models/{ llama3, llama4 }/scripts/ sub-directory. Note that the Llama4 series of models require at least 4 GPUs to run inference at full (bf16) precision.\n#!/bin/bash\nNGPUS=4\nCHECKPOINT_DIR=~/.llama/checkpoints/Llama-4-Scout-17B-16E-Instruct",
    "character_count": 993
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fd562d85-a189-420b-99e1-ff4dcd5040fe",
    "technology": "Meta Llama",
    "technology_id": "source-meta-llama",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Meta",
    "license": "Llama 3 Community License",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models",
    "path": "meta_llama/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "#!/bin/bash\nNGPUS=4\nCHECKPOINT_DIR=~/.llama/checkpoints/Llama-4-Scout-17B-16E-Instruct\nPYTHONPATH=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) \\\ntorchrun --nproc_per_node=$NGPUS \\\n-m models.llama4.scripts.chat_completion $CHECKPOINT_DIR \\\n--world_size $NGPUS\nThe above script should be used with an Instruct (Chat) model. For a Base model, update the CHECKPOINT_DIR path and use the script models.llama4.scripts.completion.\nYou can reduce the memory footprint of the models at the cost of minimal loss in accuracy by running inference with FP8 or Int4 quantization. Use the --quantization-mode flag to specify the quantization mode. There are two modes:\n- fp8_mixed : Mixed precision inference with FP8 for some weights and bfloat16 for activations.\n- int4_mixed : Mixed precision inference with Int4 for some weights and bfloat16 for activations.\nUsing FP8, running Llama-4-Scout-17B-16E-Instruct requires 2 GPUs with 80GB of memory. Using Int4, you need a single GPU with 80GB of memory.",
    "character_count": 977
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "031512b4-289a-4f2e-8a66-8f590a40e82d",
    "technology": "Meta Llama",
    "technology_id": "source-meta-llama",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Meta",
    "license": "Llama 3 Community License",
    "priority": "high",
