    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Releases: milvus-io/milvus\nRelease list\nmilvus-3.0.0\nmilvus-2.6.21\nclient/v3.0.0-beta\nclient/v3.0.0-beta\nThis is the first beta release of the Milvus Go SDK v3, targeting Milvus 3.0. It is compared against client/v2.6.5.\nThis is a beta release. APIs and protocol details may change before v3.0.0 GA.\nHighlights\n- Migrates the Go module to github.com/milvus-io/milvus/client/v3.\n- Decouples the standalone client from Milvus server-side pkg modules, substantially reducing server-only transitive dependencies.\n- Adds collection snapshot management and asynchronous restore workflows.\n- Adds read-only external collections with manual refresh support.\n- Adds search aggregation, search by primary-key IDs, query ordering, and namespace-scoped operations.\n- Adds client-side telemetry and structured RPC error inspection.\nBreaking Changes and Migration\n-\nModule path: Update all imports from: github.com/milvus-io/milvus/client/v2 to: github.com/milvus-io/milvus/client/v3\n-",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3244f08e-050b-430a-8547-0675bba844b6",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "Breaking Changes and Migration\n-\nModule path: Update all imports from: github.com/milvus-io/milvus/client/v2 to: github.com/milvus-io/milvus/client/v3\n-\nProto types: Applications directly using generated Milvus messages must migrate from milvus-proto/go-api/v2 to milvus-proto/go-api/v3. Although many high-level builders retain\nfamiliar APIs, v2 and v3 protobuf types are not interchangeable.\n-\nInstallation: go get github.com/milvus-io/milvus/client/v3@v3.0.0-beta\n-\nGo version: The module’s go directive is Go 1.24.9. The client README recommends Go 1.24.12 or later.\n-\nTelemetry behavior: Client telemetry is enabled by default. Set ClientConfig.TelemetryConfig.Enabled to false to disable heartbeat and metrics reporting.\nNew Features\n-\nCollection snapshots: Added APIs to create, drop, list, and describe collection-scoped snapshots. Snapshots can be restored asynchronously to new collections, with APIs for querying",
    "character_count": 923
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b9140bfe-ee9a-4e60-ab3a-ac7438dedab7",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "New Features\n-\nCollection snapshots: Added APIs to create, drop, list, and describe collection-scoped snapshots. Snapshots can be restored asynchronously to new collections, with APIs for querying\nand listing restore jobs. Snapshot data can also be pinned and unpinned to control garbage collection. (#44361, #48143)\n-\nExternal collections: Added schema builders for external data sources and external-field mappings:\n- Schema.WithExternalSource\n- Schema.WithExternalSpec\n- Field.WithExternalField\nExternal collections can be searched and queried using standard client APIs and refreshed through RefreshExternalCollection, GetRefreshExternalCollectionProgress, and\nListRefreshExternalCollectionJobs. (#46886, #47492, #49531)\n-\nSearch aggregation: Added bucket aggregation builders supporting multi-field keys, nested aggregations, top hits, ordering, and avg, sum, count, min, and max metrics. Results are\nreturned through ResultSet.AggregationBuckets. (#50448)\n-",
    "character_count": 963
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c40c7e55-c175-441c-8990-c1b964b8f60b",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "returned through ResultSet.AggregationBuckets. (#50448)\n-\nSearch by primary-key IDs: Added NewSearchByIDsOption and AnnRequest.WithIDs for using existing entities as vector-search inputs. Int64 and VarChar primary keys are supported.\n(#47633)\n-\nNamespace-scoped operations: Added WithNamespace support to Search, Hybrid Search, Query, iterators, Insert, Upsert, and Delete options. (#50153)\n-\nQuery ordering: Added QueryOption.WithOrderByFields, accepting expressions such as price:desc and name:asc. An explicit query limit is required when ordering is used. (#51173, #51220)\n-\nClient telemetry: Added configurable collection of request counts, errors, and latency metrics, including P99 latency, recent-error tracking, periodic server heartbeats, and server-\npushed command handling. (#47523, #47542)\n-\nStructured RPC errors: Added public RPCError, common error sentinels, ErrorCode, and IsRetryableError. RPC errors with matching Milvus codes can now be inspected using errors.Is.\n-",
    "character_count": 985
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "5b795e74-837b-49b6-b87e-b5e2ea765c96",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "-\nStructured RPC errors: Added public RPCError, common error sentinels, ErrorCode, and IsRetryableError. RPC errors with matching Milvus codes can now be inspected using errors.Is.\n-\nDynamic StructArray fields: Added Client.AddCollectionStructField and NewAddCollectionStructFieldOption, including validation and preservation of parent nullable and max_capacity\nmetadata. (#50276)\n-\nRBAC descriptions: Added user and role descriptions, role-description updates through AlterRole, and force-drop support for roles. (#50184, #50186, #47071)\n-\nImport two-phase commit: Added REST wrappers for committing or aborting bulk-import jobs through CommitImport and AbortImport. (#50177)\n-\nMessage salvage API: Added the high-level Client.DumpMessages streaming wrapper for replication and recovery workflows. (#50343, #50574)\n-\nMinHash: Added FunctionTypeMinHash support to the Go SDK function API. (#45322)\nImprovements and Bug Fixes",
    "character_count": 924
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b840668a-658c-499e-a5e2-dfcb84fd8aca",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "-\nMinHash: Added FunctionTypeMinHash support to the Go SDK function API. (#45322)\nImprovements and Bug Fixes\n- Default gRPC keepalive, reconnect, and receive-size options are now always applied before user-provided DialOptions. (#49186)\n- Row-based Insert and Upsert builders now preserve row-based processing when chaining partition, namespace, partial-update, and Array-operation options.\n- Client-local error, retry, crypto, concurrency, property, and type helpers replace the dependency on Milvus server packages.\n- Updated the v3 protobuf, gRPC, protobuf runtime, and supporting Go dependencies.\nKnown Limitations\n- This SDK release is intended for Milvus 3.0 beta and is not guaranteed to be compatible with Milvus 2.6 servers.\n- ExportSnapshot and RestoreExternalSnapshot expose preview API contracts in this release, but the server implementation currently returns Unimplemented.\n- Flush a collection before creating a snapshot if growing-segment data must be included.",
    "character_count": 977
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fcf1e0ea-9a23-416e-b238-8ae91c501df9",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "- Flush a collection before creating a snapshot if growing-segment data must be included.\n- External collections are read-only; Insert, Upsert, Delete, Import, partition management, and schema alteration are not supported.\n- Primary keys must remain unique across namespaces within the same collection because delete and upsert tombstones remain collection-scoped.\n- Search aggregation cannot be combined with legacy group-by, offsets, or search iterators. Bracketed JSON-path expressions are not yet supported.\n- Search by primary-key IDs is not supported in Hybrid Search or Search Iterator.\nmilvus-2.6.20\nv2.6.20\nRelease date: July 14, 2026\n| Milvus Version | Python SDK Version | Node.js SDK Version | Java SDK Version | Go SDK Version |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.6.20 | 2.6.16 | 2.6.17 | 2.6.22 | 2.6.20 |",
    "character_count": 810
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a22a2745-263c-463a-995e-2ea69a6b5bdc",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "Release date: July 14, 2026\n| Milvus Version | Python SDK Version | Node.js SDK Version | Java SDK Version | Go SDK Version |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.6.20 | 2.6.16 | 2.6.17 | 2.6.22 | 2.6.20 |\nWe are excited to announce the release of Milvus v2.6.20! This release improves query scheduling and batching, index loading, filtering performance, streaming rebalancing, and observability. It also resolves correctness and reliability issues across JSON filtering, streaming recovery, text indexing, analyzer configuration, and GPU_CAGRA operations.\nImprovements\n- Added named C++ thread-pool activity metrics and Grafana monitoring (#50299)\n- Improved QueryCoord scheduling by decoupling task dispatch from distribution polling to allow independent scheduling intervals (#50774, #50777)\n- Improved QueryNode query batching by increasing the default NQ grouping limits for larger merged query batches (#50859, #50898)",
    "character_count": 913
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "af8fdf9e-3a78-43fe-a2b5-b186c6b2ba8a",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "- Improved QueryNode query batching by increasing the default NQ grouping limits for larger merged query batches (#50859, #50898)\n- Improved index-loading resilience by safely completing pending range reads after partial failures (#50937)\n- Optimized VARCHAR primary-key population when loading sealed segments (#51063)\n- Improved filter execution performance by skipping null-bitmap processing for all-valid results (#51067)\n- Improved channel balancing by enabling the channel-level score balancer by default and introducing a safer default threshold for channel-exclusive mode (#51132)\n- Improved streaming rebalancing to trigger immediately when the primary resource group configuration changed (#51147)\n- Upgraded Knowhere to v2.6.17 to prevent GPU_CAGRA operations from failing with bad_optional_access under the default ef configuration (#51209)\nBug fixes\n- Fixed incorrect JSON path filter results for missing, null, or type-mismatched values (#50722, #50723)",
    "character_count": 967
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3fce761f-a91b-4075-866a-10e71df2afd3",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": "Bug fixes\n- Fixed incorrect JSON path filter results for missing, null, or type-mismatched values (#50722, #50723)\n- Fixed an issue where Marisa string indexes could fail to upload or load when the local temporary directory was missing (#50772)\n- Fixed an issue where stale streaming writes could retry indefinitely after their target collection or partition was dropped (#50849, #50895)\n- Fixed an issue where cluster-level load configuration could override user-specified collection replica settings without force override enabled (#50860)\n- Fixed an issue where analyzer runtime settings and YAML updates were not applied to the Rust analyzer layer (#50998)\n- Fixed an issue where StorageV2 text index builds could use incorrect paths for existing segment insert logs (#51002)\n- Fixed an issue where DumpMessages omitted transaction data messages and produced incomplete exports (#51102)",
    "character_count": 890
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "54c5a6cf-1208-48f3-b711-6acc72c77b49",
    "technology": "Milvus",
