    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "- Fixed an issue where DumpMessages omitted transaction data messages and produced incomplete exports (#51102)\n- Fixed an issue where ARRAY containment expressions could return incorrect results for float literals (#51130)\n- Fixed an issue where filters on missing nested JSON values, failed JSON casts, or out-of-range array elements could return incorrect results instead of UNKNOWN (#51135)\n- Fixed an issue where streaming recovery could omit physical channels recorded in collection metadata and leave required WAL topics unavailable after startup (#51144)\nmilvus-2.6.19\nv2.6.19\nRelease date: July 1, 2026\n| Milvus Version | Python SDK Version | Node.js SDK Version | Java SDK Version | Go SDK Version |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.6.19 | 2.6.16 | 2.6.17 | 2.6.22 | 2.6.19 |",
    "character_count": 777
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0dc66655-afcb-4e83-be6b-1fa87d2122a4",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "text": "Release date: July 1, 2026\n| Milvus Version | Python SDK Version | Node.js SDK Version | Java SDK Version | Go SDK Version |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.6.19 | 2.6.16 | 2.6.17 | 2.6.22 | 2.6.19 |\nWe are excited to announce the release of Milvus v2.6.19! This release improves text indexing, JSON handling, GPU runtime compatibility, RBAC metadata, and search result serialization. It also fixes correctness and stability issues across WAL recovery, scalar expressions, nullable fields, ArrayOfVector, group-by search, and DataCoord GC.\nImprovements\n- Added configurable concurrency for function runner text tokenization (#50115)\n- Improved mix compaction by building text indexes inline to avoid slow QueryNode fallback index creation (#50160)\n- Upgraded GPU Docker images to CUDA 12.9.1 for Ubuntu 22.04 builds and runtime (#50250)\n- Added a configuration option for maximum array capacity (#50265)",
    "character_count": 897
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "7b3c07de-6961-4004-9a04-504cdd8fb7a0",
    "technology": "Milvus",
    "technology_id": "source-milvus",
    "category": "vectordbs",
    "organization": "Zilliz / LF AI & Data Foundation",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/releases",
    "path": "milvus/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "text": "- Upgraded GPU Docker images to CUDA 12.9.1 for Ubuntu 22.04 builds and runtime (#50250)\n- Added a configuration option for maximum array capacity (#50265)\n- Improved S3 PutObject compatibility with OpenSSL FIPS mode by forcing CRC32C checksums (#50360, #50477)\n- Added RBAC role description support across clients, APIs, and role metadata (#50526, #50535)\n- Improved error handling by standardizing on merr with system and input error classification across Milvus (#50545)\n- Optimized null predicate evaluation for sealed chunked fields (#50586)\n- Improved JSON field handling by enabling JSON shredding by default (#50706)\n- Reduced search result serialization overhead by adding an optional zero-copy path for passing search results (#50713, #50756)\nBug fixes\n- Fixed an issue where RBAC grantee identifiers could collide due to truncated ID hashes (#50236)\n- Fixed an issue where Kafka and RMQ WAL recovery could fail to restore checkpoints with negative sentinel message IDs (#50242)",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "9d503520-e944-43bd-a43e-ea87617168cc",
