    "path": "nomic_embed/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "- Training Sparse Mixture Of Experts Text Embedding Models by Zach Nussbaum and Brandon Duderstadt\nThe contrastors library relies on custom kernels from the Flash Attention repository. To setup your enviornment you will need to follow the steps below.\nMake sure that you have Cuda 11.8+. You can check this by running nvcc --version or if you already have torch installed you can run python -c \"import torch; print(torch.version.cuda)\"\nCreate a python venv and activate it\npython3 -m venv env\nsource env/bin/activate\nInstall torch. See the torch docs for specific instructions for your system (e.g. the default CUDA torch supports is 12.1 as of 12/12/2023).\npip3 install torch torchvision torchaudio\nInstall wheel, packaging, ninja for Flash Attention (so the builds don't take too long)\npip install wheel packaging ninja setuptools\nInstall Flash Attention and the custom kernels",
    "character_count": 879
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d1d558e0-1bdf-430e-9702-c31e11214a56",
    "technology": "Nomic Embed",
    "technology_id": "source-nomic-embed",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "Nomic AI",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/nomic-ai/contrastors",
    "path": "nomic_embed/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "Install wheel, packaging, ninja for Flash Attention (so the builds don't take too long)\npip install wheel packaging ninja setuptools\nInstall Flash Attention and the custom kernels\npip install --no-cache-dir flash-attn --no-build-isolation git+https://github.com/HazyResearch/flash-attention.git#subdirectory=csrc/rotary git+https://github.com/HazyResearch/flash-attention.git#subdirectory=csrc/layer_norm git+https://github.com/HazyResearch/flash-attention.git#subdirectory=csrc/fused_dense_lib git+https://github.com/HazyResearch/flash-attention.git#subdirectory=csrc/xentropy\nInstall the rest of the requirements and the package\npip install -e . We provide access to the nomic-embed-text-v1 dataset via the nomic package. To access the data, you will need to create an account and login to the nomic package. First create an account at atlas.nomic.ai, download the nomic Python client, and run the following commands:\npip install nomic\nnomic login # follow prompts to login",
    "character_count": 975
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ff62b90d-852e-457e-bf4b-82a09d6b6946",
    "technology": "Nomic Embed",
    "technology_id": "source-nomic-embed",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "Nomic AI",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/nomic-ai/contrastors",
    "path": "nomic_embed/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "pip install nomic\nnomic login # follow prompts to login\npython -c \"from nomic import atlas; print(atlas._get_datastream_credentials(name='contrastors'))\"\nwhich will print out your access keys. You can then configure them by using aws configure or setting\nthe AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY environment variables.\nIf you do not have the AWS CLI installed, you can install it here.\nTo verify your access, you can run the following command to list the contents of the bucket:\naws s3 ls --endpoint-url=https://9fa58365a1a3d032127970d0bd9a1290.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/ s3://contrastive\naws s3 ls --endpoint-url=https://9fa58365a1a3d032127970d0bd9a1290.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/ s3://contrastive-index-filtered\nYou should be able to see the contents of the bucket and download the data.\nIf you intend to train using our data and the contrastors repo, you will need to setup fsspec support for Cloudflare R2. To do so,\ncreate a file ~/.config/fsspec/s3.json with the following contents:\n{",
