    "path": "openai_gpt/api_reference.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "- x-ratelimit-limit-project-tokens\n- x-ratelimit-remaining-project-tokens\n- x-ratelimit-reset-project-tokens\nProject-token headers may be present when a project-scoped token limit applies.\nOpenAI recommends logging request IDs in production deployments for more efficient troubleshooting with the support team, should the need arise. Official client libraries provide a property on top-level response objects containing the value of the x-request-id header.\nSupplying your own request ID with X-Client-Request-Id\nSection titled “Supplying your own request ID with X-Client-Request-Id”\nAlong with the server-generated x-request-id, you can supply your own unique identifier for each request via the X-Client-Request-Id request header. This header isn’t added automatically; you must explicitly set it on the request.\nWhen you include X-Client-Request-Id:\n-",
    "character_count": 855
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "05e77143-0c89-49cb-8b57-a1724a935733",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "api_reference",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference",
    "path": "openai_gpt/api_reference.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "When you include X-Client-Request-Id:\n-\nYou control the ID format (for example, a UUID or your internal trace ID), but it must contain only ASCII characters and be no more than 512 characters long; otherwise, the request will fail with a 400 error. Make this value unique per request.\n-\nOpenAI logs this value internally for supported endpoints, including chat/completions, embeddings, responses, and more.\n-\nIn cases like timeouts or network issues when you can’t get the X-Request-Id response header, you can share theX-Client-Request-Id value with the support team to look up whether OpenAI received the request and when.\nExample:\ncurl https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY\" \\\n-H \"X-Client-Request-Id: 123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000\"\nBackwards compatibility\nSection titled “Backwards compatibility”\nOpenAI provides stability to API users by avoiding breaking changes in major API versions whenever reasonably possible. This includes:",
    "character_count": 991
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3e6885e0-f9c4-4522-a824-2140fffda4ef",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
