    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Changelog\nJuly, 2026\nStarting July 30, GPT-5.6 Luna costs 80% less, while GPT-5.6 Terra costs 20% less. See pricing details.\nWe're also introducing Fast mode in the API, which replaces our Priority Processing offering. For GPT-5.6 Sol, Fast mode now delivers up to 2.5× faster speeds than standard processing at twice the price. This change is backward compatible: requests tagged priority will automatically use Fast mode.\nReleased the official OpenAI Terraform provider for managing OpenAI API Platform resources as infrastructure as code.\nProvision and manage projects, users, groups, roles, access assignments, service accounts, certificates, invitations, and project-level rate limits. Use standard Terraform workflows to review and apply changes, import existing resources, and detect and reconcile configuration drift. Install the provider from the Terraform Registry.",
    "character_count": 875
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "4769e2d6-d7d2-47a6-bcc1-2a70b5111e64",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "Released GPT Transcribe for accurate file transcription and final transcripts of committed Realtime turns, along with GPT Live Transcribe for low-latency streaming transcription.\nBoth models support free-form transcription context, keyword hints, and multiple expected input languages. Compare supported outputs and workflows in the transcription guide.\nAdded hard spend limits for organizations and projects on the OpenAI API platform. Set a monthly cap that causes affected API requests to return a 429 error when tracked spend reaches the limit. Use spend alerts for notification before traffic is interrupted. Read more in the spend limits guide.\nReleased the GPT-5.6 model family, including GPT-5.6 Sol for frontier capability, GPT-5.6 Terra for a balance of intelligence and cost, and GPT-5.6 Luna for efficient, high-volume workloads. The gpt-5.6 alias routes requests to gpt-5.6-sol.",
    "character_count": 891
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8594f298-7247-42a7-8888-3bf1e89e8826",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "GPT-5.6 adds Programmatic Tool Calling, explicit prompt caching controls, persisted reasoning, max reasoning effort, and Pro mode, and Multi-agent orchestration in beta for the Responses API. GPT-5.6 also accepts images at their original dimensions with original or auto image detail.\nReleased GPT-Realtime-2.1, an updated realtime reasoning model with improved alphanumeric recognition, silence and noise handling, and interruption behavior. Also released GPT-Realtime-2.1 mini, a faster, lower-cost distilled reasoning model for realtime voice applications.\nJune, 2026\nUpdated the chat-latest snapshot, which points to the latest Instant model currently used in ChatGPT. We recommend leveraging GPT-5.5 for production API usage, but feel free to use this model to test the latest improvements for chat use cases. The underlying model snapshot will be regularly updated. Read more here.",
    "character_count": 887
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "cd5e4316-346b-43ff-aeb0-c6b2cd6e2b2b",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "Released the Safety Usage Dashboard on the OpenAI API platform. The Safety dashboard shows blocked Responses requests based on safety_identifier values sent on requests to identify end users. Visit the Safety dashboard.\nWeb search can now return image results alongside regular text results. Use image search when your application needs current or web-grounded visuals, such as product photos, landmarks, places, events, or visual references. Read more in the web search guide.\nReleased a redesigned navigation for the OpenAI API platform, visit here.\nAdded moderation scores to the Responses API and Chat Completions API. Pass a moderation object in a generation request to receive moderation results for both the model input and generated output in the same response.\nLearn more in the Moderation guide.\nAnnounced the deprecation of reusable prompt objects, the Evals platform, and Agent Builder. See the deprecations page for shutdown timelines and migration guidance.",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b7ec71ce-56ff-4be2-ab4c-585c3aefbb59",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "Announced the deprecation of reusable prompt objects, the Evals platform, and Agent Builder. See the deprecations page for shutdown timelines and migration guidance.\nStarting June 2, 2026, eligible container sessions will be billed per minute with a 5-minute minimum, instead of being billed at the full 20-minute session rate. The underlying per-minute rate will remain the same.\nThis update is intended to make billing more granular for shorter sessions and will lower effective cost for customers.\nYou can find current built-in tool pricing in our API pricing docs.\nOpenAI models are now available in Amazon Bedrock through an OpenAI-compatible Responses API endpoint. Supported models and features vary by AWS Region. Learn more.\nMay, 2026\nFor organizations without ZDR enabled, prompt_cache_retention now defaults to 24h instead of in_memory, enabling extended prompt caching by default. Learn more.",
    "character_count": 904
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "58e429a3-da41-4048-ba16-3bdf05fff67f",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "May, 2026\nFor organizations without ZDR enabled, prompt_cache_retention now defaults to 24h instead of in_memory, enabling extended prompt caching by default. Learn more.\nReleased chat-latest snapshot which points to the latest Instant model currently used in ChatGPT. We recommend leveraging GPT-5.5 for production API usage, but feel free to use this model to test the latest improvements for chat use cases. The underlying model snapshot will be regularly updated. Read more here.\nReleased workload identity federation. Trusted workloads can exchange externally issued identity tokens for short-lived OpenAI access tokens without storing long-lived API keys.\nAdded new Admin API capabilities for managing spend alerts, model allowlists, data retention settings, and hosted tool permissions, plus querying granular billing line items.",
    "character_count": 836
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "233354ef-1080-4776-92e7-e52c390579fc",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "Added new Admin API capabilities for managing spend alerts, model allowlists, data retention settings, and hosted tool permissions, plus querying granular billing line items.\nReleased Secure MCP Tunnel for enterprise customers. Secure MCP Tunnel lets supported OpenAI products including ChatGPT web, Codex, Responses API, and AgentKit connect to private or on-prem MCP servers through a customer-hosted tunnel-client without exposing those servers to the public internet.\nYou can now manage multiple IP allowlists and apply each one at the project level or across the whole organization. To configure them, go to Settings > Security > IP allowlist.\nDeprecated DALL·E model snapshots and the Realtime API Beta.\nDALL·E model snapshots dall-e-2 and dall-e-3 were deprecated and removed from the API on May 12, 2026. We recommend using gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, or gpt-image-1-mini instead.",
    "character_count": 886
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "17b6be1d-22e3-4fb8-b310-4797a14880d1",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "DALL·E model snapshots dall-e-2 and dall-e-3 were deprecated and removed from the API on May 12, 2026. We recommend using gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, or gpt-image-1-mini instead.\nThe Realtime API Beta was deprecated and removed from the API on May 12, 2026. If you are still using the beta interface, migrate to the released Realtime API. See the migration guide and the full deprecations page.\nAdded return_token_budget for the Responses API web search tool. Use it to opt in to longer GPT-5+ reasoning web search runs for high-effort research and evaluation workloads.\nReleased GPT-Realtime-2, a new realtime voice model with configurable reasoning for speech-to-speech agents, along with GPT-Realtime-Translate for streaming speech translation and GPT-Realtime-Whisper for streaming speech-to-text.",
    "character_count": 799
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a8cabaae-71a9-492e-8783-30a116f6c23e",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "Updated the Realtime and audio guide, added a dedicated Realtime translation guide, refreshed Realtime transcription for streaming transcripts, and moved realtime prompting guidance into Using realtime models.\nReleased the OpenAI Developers plugin for Codex. This helps you build AI applications and agents in Codex with OpenAI Platform access and OpenAI API setup guidance.\nThe updated Agents SDK is now available in TypeScript, with support for sandbox agents and an open-source harness built in. Learn more here.\nReleased chat-latest snapshot which points to the latest Instant model currently used in ChatGPT. We recommend leveraging GPT-5.5 for production API usage, but feel free to use this model to test our latest improvements for chat use cases. The underlying model snapshot will be regularly updated. Read more here.\nAdmin APIs are now supported in the OpenAI SDKs for Node, Python, Go, Ruby, and Java. See the Admin APIs guide for setup instructions and examples.\nApril, 2026",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0d8c02fb-637d-43db-bfad-88d5b62d94e5",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": "Admin APIs are now supported in the OpenAI SDKs for Node, Python, Go, Ruby, and Java. See the Admin APIs guide for setup instructions and examples.\nApril, 2026\nReleased GPT-5.5, a new frontier model for complex professional work, to the Chat Completions and Responses API, and released GPT-5.5 Pro for Responses API requests for tougher problems that benefit from more compute.\nGPT-5.5 supports a 1M token context window, image input, structured outputs, function calling, prompt caching, Batch, tool search, built-in computer use, hosted shell, apply patch, Skills, MCP, and web search. Key updates include:\n- Reasoning effort now defaults to medium .\n- When image_detail is unset or set toauto , the model now uses original behavior.\n- Caching for GPT-5.5 only works with extended prompt caching. In-memory prompt caching is not supported. Learn more here.",
    "character_count": 858
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c212c201-0726-44a9-8181-2763a85964df",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "- Caching for GPT-5.5 only works with extended prompt caching. In-memory prompt caching is not supported. Learn more here.\nReleased GPT Image 2, a state-of-the-art image generation model for image generation and editing. GPT Image 2 supports flexible image sizes, high-fidelity image inputs, token-based image pricing, and Batch API support with a 50% discount.\nUpdated the Agents SDK with new capabilities, including:\n- running agents in controlled sandboxes;\n- inspecting and customizing the open-source harness; and\n- controlling when memories are created and where they're stored.\nMarch, 2026\nReleased GPT-5.4 mini and GPT-5.4 nano to the Chat Completions and Responses API. GPT-5.4 mini brings GPT-5.4-class capabilities to a faster, more efficient model for high-volume workloads, while GPT-5.4 nano is optimized for simple high-volume tasks where speed and cost matter most.",
    "character_count": 881
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "984233a0-33af-4ef6-a534-7b76872faaa1",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "text": "GPT-5.4 mini supports tool search, built-in computer use, and compaction. GPT-5.4 nano supports compaction, but does not support tool search or computer use.\nUpdated the gpt-5.3-chat-latest slug to point to the latest model currently used in ChatGPT.\nUpdated our image encoder to fix a small bug with input_image inputs in GPT-5.4. Some image understanding use cases may now see improved quality. No action is required.\nExpanded the Sora API with reusable character references, longer generations up to 20 seconds, 1080p output for sora-2-pro, video extensions, and Batch API support for POST /v1/videos. 1080p generations on sora-2-pro are billed at $0.70 per second. Learn more here.\nAdded POST /v1/videos/edits for editing existing videos. This will replace POST /v1/videos/{video_id}/remix, which will be deprecated in 6 months. Learn more here.",
    "character_count": 849
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a24f71a0-29db-41ca-bfb3-e3596e25651c",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "text": "Added POST /v1/videos/edits for editing existing videos. This will replace POST /v1/videos/{video_id}/remix, which will be deprecated in 6 months. Learn more here.\nReleased GPT-5.4, our newest frontier model for professional work, to the Chat Completions and Responses API, and released GPT-5.4 Pro to the Responses API for tougher problems that benefit from more compute.\nAlso released:\n- Tool search in the Responses API, which lets models defer large tool surfaces until runtime to reduce token usage, preserve cache performance, and improve latency.\n- Built-in Computer use support in GPT-5.4 through the Responses API computer tool for screenshot-based UI interaction.\n- A 1M token context window and native Compaction support for longer-running agent workflows.\nReleased gpt-5.3-chat-latest to the Chat Completions and Responses API. This model points to the GPT-5.3 Instant snapshot currently used in ChatGPT. Read more here.\nFebruary, 2026",
    "character_count": 947
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "926d64a7-e3b1-4568-8b8e-9e961f19fbeb",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "text": "Released gpt-5.3-chat-latest to the Chat Completions and Responses API. This model points to the GPT-5.3 Instant snapshot currently used in ChatGPT. Read more here.\nFebruary, 2026\nExpanded input_file support to accept more document, presentation, spreadsheet, code, and text file types. Learn more here.\nReleased phase to the Responses API. It labels an assistant message as intermediate commentary (commentary) or the final answer (final_answer). Read more here.\nReleased gpt-5.3-codex to the Responses API. Read more here.\nLaunched WebSocket mode for the Responses API. Learn more here.\nReleased GPT-Realtime-1.5 to the Realtime API.\nReleased gpt-audio-1.5 to the Chat Completions API. Read more here.\nBatch API is now supported for GPT Image models: gpt-image-1.5, chatgpt-image-latest, gpt-image-1, and gpt-image-1-mini.\nUpdated the gpt-5.2-chat-latest slug to point to the latest model currently used in ChatGPT.\nLaunched server-side compaction in the Responses API.",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "526ef22b-6b26-425e-9fbc-9ae411ea76ab",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "text": "Updated the gpt-5.2-chat-latest slug to point to the latest model currently used in ChatGPT.\nLaunched server-side compaction in the Responses API.\nLaunched support for Skills in the Responses API. We support Skills across both local execution and hosted container-based execution.\nLaunched a new Hosted Shell tool, as well as support for networking in containers.\nAdded support for application/json requests on /v1/images/edits for GPT image models. JSON requests use images (and optional mask) with image_url or file_id references instead of multipart uploads.\nWe have optimized our inference stack for API customers and GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex now run ~40% faster. Model and model weights are unchanged.\nJanuary, 2026\nAnnounced Open Responses: an open-source spec for building multi-provider, interoperable LLM interfaces built on top of the original OpenAI Responses API.",
    "character_count": 876
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b2fa85e7-9d7f-4895-b271-51188758e444",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "text": "January, 2026\nAnnounced Open Responses: an open-source spec for building multi-provider, interoperable LLM interfaces built on top of the original OpenAI Responses API.\nReleased gpt-5.2-codex to the Responses API. GPT-5.2-Codex is a version of GPT-5.2 optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. Read more here.\nAdded dedicated SIP IP ranges for Realtime API. sip.api.openai.com does GeoIP routing, and will direct SIP traffic to the closest region. Learn more.\nUpdated the gpt-realtime-mini and gpt-audio-mini slugs to point to the 2025-12-15 snapshots. If you need the previous model snapshots, use gpt-realtime-mini-2025-10-06 and gpt-audio-mini-2025-10-06.\nUpdated the sora-2 slug to point to sora-2-2025-12-08. If you need the previous model snapshot, use sora-2-2025-10-06.",
    "character_count": 804
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3d1da901-4931-4f3d-b199-fbeb7056fc85",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
    "license": "Proprietary",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "text": "Updated the sora-2 slug to point to sora-2-2025-12-08. If you need the previous model snapshot, use sora-2-2025-10-06.\nUpdated the gpt-4o-mini-tts and gpt-4o-mini-transcribe slugs to point to the 2025-12-15 snapshots. If you need the previous model snapshots, use gpt-4o-mini-tts-2025-03-20 and gpt-4o-mini-transcribe-2025-03-20. We currently recomend using gpt-4o-mini-transcribe over gpt-4o-transcribe for the best results.\nFixed an issue where gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest were incorrectly using high fidelity for image edits through /v1/images/edits, even when fidelity was explicitly set to low (the default).\nDecember, 2025\nAdded gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest to the Responses API image generation tool.\nReleased gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest, our latest and most advanced models for image generation. Read more here.",
    "character_count": 851
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "345e5ca5-fa93-4c9e-9d11-5a7d00dd6336",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
