    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "text": "Released IP allowlist. IP allowlisting restricts API access to only the IP addresses or ranges you specify.\nSeptember, 2025\nAdded support for image and file as a tool call output in Responses API.\nLaunched special-purpose model gpt-5-codex, built and optimized for use with the Codex CLI.\nAugust, 2025\nThe OpenAI Realtime API is now generally available. Learn more in our Realtime API guide.\nAdded support for connectors to the Responses API. Connectors are OpenAI-maintained MCP wrappers for popular services like Google apps, Dropbox, and more that can be used to give model read access to data stored in those services.\nReleased the Conversations API, which allows you to create and manage long-running conversations with the Responses API. See the migration guide to see a side-by-side comparison and learn how to migrate from an Assistants API integration to Responses and Conversations.\nReleased GPT-5 family of models in the API, including gpt-5, gpt-5-mini, and gpt-5-nano.",
    "character_count": 981
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "7543c32f-f41c-40a1-8b83-571a6088ee8b",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "OpenAI",
