    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/changelog",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "text": "Added metadata field support to fine-tuning jobs.\nFebruary, 2025\nReleased a research preview of GPT-4.5—our largest and most capable chat model yet. GPT-4.5's high \"EQ\" and understanding of user intent make it better at creative tasks and agentic planning.\nLaunched the API Usage Dashboard Update. This update addresses requests for additional data filters, such as project selection, date picker, and fine-grained intervals. There’s also better support for viewing usage across different products and service tiers.\nIntroducing data residency in Europe. Read more here.\nJanuary, 2025\nLaunched o3-mini, a new small reasoning model that is optimized for science, math, and coding tasks.\nExpanded access to o1 model. The o1 series of models are trained with reinforcement learning to perform complex reasoning.\nDecember, 2024\nLaunched Admin API Key Rotations, enabling customers to programmatically rotate their admin api keys.",
    "character_count": 925
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a70b0f7d-132c-4cfc-abc8-8d29477ae5a4",
    "technology": "OpenAI GPT",
    "technology_id": "source-openai-gpt",
    "category": "llms",
