    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/peft",
    "path": "peft/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "model = PeftModel.from_pretrained(model, \"qwen2.5-3b-lora\")\ninputs = tokenizer(\"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees and place the cookie dough\", return_tensors=\"pt\")\noutputs = model.generate(**inputs.to(device), max_new_tokens=50)\nprint(tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True))\n# prints something like: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees and place the cookie dough in a baking dish [...]\nThere are many benefits of using PEFT but the main one is the huge savings in compute and storage, making PEFT applicable to many different use cases.\nConsider the memory requirements for training the following models on the ought/raft/twitter_complaints dataset with an A100 80GB GPU with more than 64GB of CPU RAM.\n| Model | Full Finetuning | PEFT-LoRA PyTorch | PEFT-LoRA DeepSpeed with CPU Offloading |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| bigscience/T0_3B (3B params) | 47.14GB GPU / 2.96GB CPU | 14.4GB GPU / 2.96GB CPU | 9.8GB GPU / 17.8GB CPU |",
    "character_count": 931
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "db7a7a5a-4e62-46e0-add5-e157b7dd9ef3",
    "technology": "PEFT",
    "technology_id": "source-peft",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/peft",
    "path": "peft/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "|---|---|---|---|\n| bigscience/T0_3B (3B params) | 47.14GB GPU / 2.96GB CPU | 14.4GB GPU / 2.96GB CPU | 9.8GB GPU / 17.8GB CPU |\n| bigscience/mt0-xxl (12B params) | OOM GPU | 56GB GPU / 3GB CPU | 22GB GPU / 52GB CPU |\n| bigscience/bloomz-7b1 (7B params) | OOM GPU | 32GB GPU / 3.8GB CPU | 18.1GB GPU / 35GB CPU |\nWith LoRA you can fully finetune a 12B parameter model that would've otherwise run out of memory on the 80GB GPU, and comfortably fit and train a 3B parameter model. When you look at the 3B parameter model's performance, it is comparable to a fully finetuned model at a fraction of the GPU memory.\n| Submission Name | Accuracy |\n|---|---|\n| Human baseline (crowdsourced) | 0.897 |\n| Flan-T5 | 0.892 |\n| lora-t0-3b | 0.863 |\nTip",
    "character_count": 740
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0633288a-c9d4-4375-ac1b-949a7d04b38a",
    "technology": "PEFT",
    "technology_id": "source-peft",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Hugging Face",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
