    "path": "promptfoo/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "- Open-source: LLM evals are a commodity and should be served by 100% open-source projects with no strings attached.\n- Private: This software runs completely locally. The evals run on your machine and talk directly with the LLM.\nWorkflow and philosophy\nTest-driven prompt engineering is much more effective than trial-and-error.\nSerious LLM development requires a systematic approach to prompt engineering. Promptfoo streamlines the process of evaluating and improving language model performance.\n- Define test cases: Identify core use cases and failure modes. Prepare a set of prompts and test cases that represent these scenarios.\n- Configure evaluation: Set up your evaluation by specifying prompts, test cases, and API providers.\n- Run evaluation: Use the command-line tool or library to execute the evaluation and record model outputs for each prompt.",
    "character_count": 856
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "4bd81337-1703-4de9-9433-76f20888b244",
