    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "- Deployment: the demonstration of how to deploy Qwen for large-scale inference with frameworks like SGLang, vLLM, TGI, etc.;\n- Quantization: the practice of quantizing LLMs with GPTQ, AWQ, as well as the guidance for how to make high-quality quantized GGUF files;\n- Training: the instructions for post-training, including SFT and RLHF (TODO) with frameworks like Axolotl, LLaMA-Factory, etc.\n- Framework: the usage of Qwen with frameworks for application, e.g., RAG, Agent, etc.\nOver the past three months, we continued to explore the potential of the Qwen3 families and we are excited to introduce the updated Qwen3-2507 in two variants, Qwen3-Instruct-2507 and Qwen3-Thinking-2507, and three sizes, 235B-A22B, 30B-A3B, and 4B.\nQwen3-Instruct-2507 is the updated version of the previous Qwen3 non-thinking mode, featuring the following key enhancements:",
    "character_count": 855
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "77db6dcb-6668-4ef2-855c-bbaba90eb207",
    "technology": "Qwen",
    "technology_id": "source-qwen",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Alibaba Cloud",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
