    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "text": "To pull a model checkpoint and run the model, use the ollama run command. You can specify a model size by adding a suffix to qwen3, such as :8b or :30b-a3b:\nollama run qwen3:8b\n# Setting parameters, type \"/set parameter num_ctx 40960\" and \"/set parameter num_predict 32768\"\n# To exit, type \"/bye\" and press ENTER\n# For Qwen3-2504 models,\n# - To enable thinking, which is the default, type \"/set think\"\n# - To disable thinking, type \"/set nothink\"\nYou can also access the Ollama service via its OpenAI-compatible API.\nPlease note that you need to (1) keep ollama serve running while using the API, and (2) execute ollama run qwen3:8b before utilizing this API to ensure that the model checkpoint is prepared.\nThe API is at http://localhost:11434/v1/ by default.\nFor additional details, please visit ollama.ai.\nNote\nOllama's naming may not be consistent with the Qwen's original naming.\nFor example, qwen3:30b-a3b in Ollama points to qwen3:30b-a3b-thinking-2507-q4_K_M as of August 2025.",
    "character_count": 985
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "04a2564d-7226-4605-a35d-a592323cfcba",
    "technology": "Qwen",
    "technology_id": "source-qwen",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Alibaba Cloud",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5",
    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "text": "Note\nOllama's naming may not be consistent with the Qwen's original naming.\nFor example, qwen3:30b-a3b in Ollama points to qwen3:30b-a3b-thinking-2507-q4_K_M as of August 2025.\nPlease check https://ollama.com/library/qwen3/tags before use.\nNote\nOllama adopts the same \"rotating context management\" with llama.cpp.\nHowever, its default settings (num_ctx 2048 and num_predict -1), suggesting infinite generation with a 2048-token context,\ncould lead to trouble for Qwen3 models.\nWe recommend setting num_ctx and num_predict properly.\nQwen3 has already been supported by lmstudio.ai. You can directly use LMStudio with our GGUF files.\nTo export and run on ExecuTorch (iOS, Android, Mac, Linux, and more), please follow this example.\nTo export and run on MNN, which supports Qwen3 on mobile devices, please visit Alibaba MNN.\nIf you are running on Apple Silicon, mlx-lm also supports Qwen3 (mlx-lm>=0.24.0).\nLook for models ending with MLX on Hugging Face Hub.",
    "character_count": 956
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "5670cf57-0203-4213-84ae-9e74266acc42",
    "technology": "Qwen",
    "technology_id": "source-qwen",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Alibaba Cloud",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5",
    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "text": "If you are running on Apple Silicon, mlx-lm also supports Qwen3 (mlx-lm>=0.24.0).\nLook for models ending with MLX on Hugging Face Hub.\nIf you are running on Intel CPU or GPU, OpenVINO toolkit supports Qwen3. You can follow this chatbot example.\nQwen3 is supported by multiple inference frameworks.\nHere we demonstrate the usage of SGLang, vLLM and TensorRT-LLM.\nYou can also find Qwen3 models from various inference providers, e.g., Alibaba Cloud Model Studio.\nSGLang is a fast serving framework for large language models and vision language models.\nSGLang could be used to launch a server with OpenAI-compatible API service.\nsglang>=0.4.6.post1 is required.\nFor Qwen3-Instruct-2507,\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 --port 30000 --context-length 262144\nFor Qwen3-Thinking-2507,\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Thinking-2507 --port 30000 --context-length 262144 --reasoning-parser deepseek-r1\nFor Qwen3, it is",
    "character_count": 984
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "88095751-d892-4438-8554-7056c9047f7c",
    "technology": "Qwen",
    "technology_id": "source-qwen",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Alibaba Cloud",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5",
    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "text": "For Qwen3-Thinking-2507,\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Thinking-2507 --port 30000 --context-length 262144 --reasoning-parser deepseek-r1\nFor Qwen3, it is\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 30000 --context-length 131072 --reasoning-parser qwen3\nAn OpenAI-compatible API will be available at http://localhost:30000/v1.\nNote\nDue to the preprocessing of API requests in SGLang, which drops all reasoning_content fields, the quality of multi-step tool use with Qwen3 thinking models may be suboptimal, which requires the existence of the related thinking content. While the fixes are being worked on, as a workdaround, we recommend passing the content as it is, without extracting thinking content, and the chat template will correctly handle the processing.\nvLLM is a high-throughput and memory-efficient inference and serving engine for LLMs.\nvllm>=0.9.0 is recommended.\nFor Qwen3-Instruct-2507,",
    "character_count": 955
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f492bd6b-a687-4205-9857-4edc686582bc",
    "technology": "Qwen",
    "technology_id": "source-qwen",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Alibaba Cloud",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5",
    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "text": "vLLM is a high-throughput and memory-efficient inference and serving engine for LLMs.\nvllm>=0.9.0 is recommended.\nFor Qwen3-Instruct-2507,\nvllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 --port 8000 --max-model-len 262144\nFor Qwen3-Thinking-2507,\nvllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Thinking-2507 --port 8000 --max-model-len 262144 --enable-reasoning --reasoning-parser deepseek_r1\nFor Qwen3, it is\nvllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8000 --max-model-len 131072 --enable-reasoning --reasoning-parser qwen3\nAn OpenAI-compatible API will be available at http://localhost:8000/v1.\nNote\nDue to the preprocessing of API requests in vLLM, which drops all reasoning_content fields, the quality of multi-step tool use with Qwen3 thinking models may be suboptimal, which requires the existence of the related thinking content. While the fixes are being worked on, as a workdaround, we recommend passing the content as it is, without extracting thinking content, and the chat template will correctly handle the processing.",
    "character_count": 999
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "7c8bf57c-e6c9-45f6-8f72-7533532cf263",
    "technology": "Qwen",
    "technology_id": "source-qwen",
    "category": "llms",
    "organization": "Alibaba Cloud",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5",
    "path": "qwen/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "text": "TensorRT-LLM is an open-source LLM inference engine from NVIDIA, which provides optimizations including custom attention kernels, quantization and more on NVIDIA GPUs. Qwen3 is supported in its re-architected PyTorch backend. tensorrt_llm>=0.20.0rc3 is recommended. Please refer to the README page for more details.\ntrtllm-serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --host localhost --port 8000 --backend pytorch\nAn OpenAI-compatible API will be available at http://localhost:8000/v1.\nFor deployment on Ascend NPUs, please visit Modelers and search for Qwen3.\nFor tool use capabilities, we recommend taking a look at Qwen-Agent, which provides a wrapper around these APIs to support tool use or function calling with MCP support. Tool use with Qwen3 can also be conducted with SGLang, vLLM, Transformers, llama.cpp, Ollama, etc. Follow guides in our documentation to see how to enable the support.",
    "character_count": 874
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e4a7b1ad-e58d-44be-828f-0cdf20e6be6e",
    "technology": "Qwen",
