    "chunk_index": 67,
    "text": "- start_multi_process_pool(target_devices: list[str] | None = None) dict[Literal['input', 'output', 'processes'], Any]\n- Starts a multi-process pool to infer with several independent processes. This method is recommended if you want to predict on multiple GPUs or CPUs. It is advised to start only one process per GPU. This method works together with predict and stop_multi_process_pool.\n- Parameters:\n- target_devices (List[str], optional) – PyTorch target devices, e.g. [“cuda:0”, “cuda:1”, …], [“npu:0”, “npu:1”, …], or [“cpu”, “cpu”, “cpu”, “cpu”]. If target_devices is None and CUDA/NPU is available, then all available CUDA/NPU devices will be used. If target_devices is None and CUDA/NPU is not available, then 4 CPU devices will be used.\n- Returns:\n- A dictionary with the target processes, an input queue, and an output queue.\n- Return type:\n- Dict[str, Any]",
    "character_count": 867
