    "text": "- Parameters:\n- modality – A single modality string (e.g. \"text\" ,\"image\" ) or a tuple\nof modality strings (e.g.(\"image\", \"text\") ).\n- Returns:\n- Whether the model supports the given modality.\n- Return type:\n- bool\nExample: >>> from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer >>> model = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\") >>> model.supports(\"text\") True >>> model.supports(\"image\") False\n\n- to(*args, **kwargs)\n- Moves and/or casts the parameters and buffers. This can be called as\n- to(device=None, dtype=None, non_blocking=False)\n\n- to(dtype, non_blocking=False)\n\n- to(tensor, non_blocking=False)",
