    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Pretrained Models\nWe provide various pre-trained Sentence Transformers models via our Sentence Transformers Hugging Face organization. Additionally, over 6,000 community Sentence Transformers models have been publicly released on the Hugging Face Hub. All models can be found here:\n- Original models: Sentence Transformers Hugging Face organization.\n- Community models: All Sentence Transformer models on Hugging Face.\nEach of these models can be easily downloaded and used like so:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n# Load https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2\")\nembeddings = model.encode([\n\"The weather is lovely today.\",\n\"It's so sunny outside!\",\n\"He drove to the stadium.\",\n])\nsimilarities = model.similarity(embeddings, embeddings)\nNote\nConsider using the Massive Textual Embedding Benchmark leaderboard as an inspiration of strong Sentence Transformer models. Be wary:",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "476a6d55-5ffe-47b0-abb2-dc9687042907",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "])\nsimilarities = model.similarity(embeddings, embeddings)\nNote\nConsider using the Massive Textual Embedding Benchmark leaderboard as an inspiration of strong Sentence Transformer models. Be wary:\n- Model sizes: it is recommended to filter away the large models that might not be feasible without excessive hardware.\n- Experimentation is key: models that perform well on the leaderboard do not necessarily do well on your tasks, it is crucial to experiment with various promising models.\nTip\nRead Sentence Transformer > Usage > Speeding up Inference for tips on how to speed up inference of models by up to 2x-3x.\nOriginal Models\nThe following table provides an overview of a selection of our models. They have been extensively evaluated for their quality to embedded sentences (Performance Sentence Embeddings) and to embedded search queries & paragraphs (Performance Semantic Search).",
    "character_count": 886
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b1950010-76b2-47f3-8e49-5a5b97d8715e",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "The all-* models were trained on all available training data (more than 1 billion training pairs) and are designed as general purpose models. The sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2 model provides the best quality, while sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 is 5 times faster and still offers good quality. Toggle All models to see all evaluated original models.\nSemantic Search Models\nThe following models have been specifically trained for Semantic Search: Given a question / search query, these models are able to find relevant text passages. For more details, see Usage > Semantic Search.\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/multi-qa-mpnet-base-cos-v1\")\nquery_embedding = model.encode(\"How big is London\")\npassage_embeddings = model.encode([\n\"London is known for its financial district\",\n\"London has 9,787,426 inhabitants at the 2011 census\",\n\"The United Kingdom is the fourth largest exporter of goods in the world\",\n])",
    "character_count": 999
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d2020bf5-96ab-447f-abe3-3a477a4346d6",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "\"London is known for its financial district\",\n\"London has 9,787,426 inhabitants at the 2011 census\",\n\"The United Kingdom is the fourth largest exporter of goods in the world\",\n])\nsimilarity = model.similarity(query_embedding, passage_embeddings)\n# => tensor([[0.4659, 0.6142, 0.2697]])\nMulti-QA Models\nThe following models have been trained on 215M question-answer pairs from various sources and domains, including StackExchange, Yahoo Answers, Google & Bing search queries and many more. These model perform well across many search tasks and domains.\nThese models were tuned to be used with the dot-product similarity score:\n| Model | Performance Semantic Search (6 Datasets) | Queries (GPU / CPU) per sec. |\n|---|---|---|\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-mpnet-base-dot-v1 | 57.60 | 4,000 / 170 |\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-distilbert-dot-v1 | 52.51 | 7,000 / 350 |\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-dot-v1 | 49.19 | 18,000 / 750 |",
    "character_count": 948
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3c30e48b-2f25-4586-988e-1a6e884002b3",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-distilbert-dot-v1 | 52.51 | 7,000 / 350 |\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-dot-v1 | 49.19 | 18,000 / 750 |\nThese models produce normalized vectors of length 1, which can be used with dot-product, cosine-similarity and Euclidean distance as the similarity functions:\n| Model | Performance Semantic Search (6 Datasets) | Queries (GPU / CPU) per sec. |\n|---|---|---|\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-mpnet-base-cos-v1 | 57.46 | 4,000 / 170 |\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-distilbert-cos-v1 | 52.83 | 7,000 / 350 |\n| sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1 | 51.83 | 18,000 / 750 |\nMSMARCO Passage Models\nThe following models have been trained on the MSMARCO Passage Ranking Dataset, which contains 500k real queries from Bing search together with the relevant passages from various web sources. Given the diversity of the MSMARCO dataset, models also perform well on other domains.",
    "character_count": 932
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "dc2da71d-b13d-4c5a-8e28-453964dafb36",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "These models were tuned to be used with the dot-product similarity score:\n| Model | MSMARCO MRR@10 dev set | Performance Semantic Search (6 Datasets) | Queries (GPU / CPU) per sec. |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-bert-base-dot-v5 | 38.08 | 52.11 | 4,000 / 170 |\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-distilbert-dot-v5 | 37.25 | 49.47 | 7,000 / 350 |\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-distilbert-base-tas-b | 34.43 | 49.25 | 7,000 / 350 |\nThese models produce normalized vectors of length 1, which can be used with dot-product, cosine-similarity and Euclidean distance as the similarity functions:\n| Model | MSMARCO MRR@10 dev set | Performance Semantic Search (6 Datasets) | Queries (GPU / CPU) per sec. |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-distilbert-cos-v5 | 33.79 | 44.98 | 7,000 / 350 |\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-MiniLM-L12-cos-v5 | 32.75 | 43.89 | 11,000 / 400 |\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-MiniLM-L6-cos-v5 | 32.27 | 42.16 | 18,000 / 750 |",
    "character_count": 982
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "614ab4fd-459c-443b-8894-a297cc4a68e0",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "| sentence-transformers/msmarco-MiniLM-L12-cos-v5 | 32.75 | 43.89 | 11,000 / 400 |\n| sentence-transformers/msmarco-MiniLM-L6-cos-v5 | 32.27 | 42.16 | 18,000 / 750 |\nMultilingual Models\nThe following models similar embeddings for the same texts in different languages. You do not need to specify the input language. Details are in our publication Making Monolingual Sentence Embeddings Multilingual using Knowledge Distillation. We used the following 50+ languages: ar, bg, ca, cs, da, de, el, en, es, et, fa, fi, fr, fr-ca, gl, gu, he, hi, hr, hu, hy, id, it, ja, ka, ko, ku, lt, lv, mk, mn, mr, ms, my, nb, nl, pl, pt, pt-br, ro, ru, sk, sl, sq, sr, sv, th, tr, uk, ur, vi, zh-cn, zh-tw.\nSemantic Similarity Models\nThese models find semantically similar sentences within one language or across languages:",
    "character_count": 805
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c9ac3fb1-baef-4fd3-adbf-5cd202d6f1f2",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "Semantic Similarity Models\nThese models find semantically similar sentences within one language or across languages:\n- sentence-transformers/distiluse-base-multilingual-cased-v1: Multilingual knowledge distilled version of multilingual Universal Sentence Encoder. Supports 15 languages: Arabic, Chinese, Dutch, English, French, German, Italian, Korean, Polish, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish, Turkish.\n- sentence-transformers/distiluse-base-multilingual-cased-v2: Multilingual knowledge distilled version of multilingual Universal Sentence Encoder. This version supports 50+ languages, but performs a bit weaker than the v1 model.\n- sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2 - Multilingual version of sentence-transformers/paraphrase-MiniLM-L12-v2, trained on parallel data for 50+ languages.\n- sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-mpnet-base-v2 - Multilingual version of sentence-transformers/paraphrase-mpnet-base-v2, trained on parallel data for 50+ languages.",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "33cefb46-59f2-4f16-84f8-c076527b8570",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "- sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-mpnet-base-v2 - Multilingual version of sentence-transformers/paraphrase-mpnet-base-v2, trained on parallel data for 50+ languages.\nBitext Mining\nBitext mining describes the process of finding translated sentence pairs in two languages. If this is your use-case, the following model gives the best performance:\n- sentence-transformers/LaBSE - LaBSE Model. Supports 109 languages. Works well for finding translation pairs in multiple languages. As detailed here, LaBSE works less well for assessing the similarity of sentence pairs that are not translations of each other.\nExtending a model to new languages is easy by following Training Examples > Multilingual Models.\nMultimodal Models\nSentence Transformers supports multimodal models that can embed text alongside images, audio, or video into a joint vector space. This enables cross-modal tasks like text-to-image search, image-to-image search, image clustering, and zero-shot classification.",
    "character_count": 993
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8c9b92e2-fe23-4364-ae0b-572384cd79a7",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": "See also\nSee the Multimodal Embedding & Reranker Models blogpost for an inference walkthrough and an overview of the multimodal models supported at the time of writing.\nTip\nMultimodal models require additional dependencies. Install them with e.g. pip install -U \"sentence-transformers[image]\" for image support. See Installation for all options.\nYou can check which modalities a model supports using the modalities property and supports() method:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Embedding-2B\")\nprint(model.modalities)\n# => ['text', 'image', 'video', 'message']\nprint(model.supports(\"image\"))\n# => True\nprint(model.supports(\"audio\"))\n# => False\nImage & Text Models\nImage-text models embed both images and text into the same vector space.",
    "character_count": 801
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "90a99a77-179b-4675-90c7-dd8d5346e70e",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "print(model.supports(\"image\"))\n# => True\nprint(model.supports(\"audio\"))\n# => False\nImage & Text Models\nImage-text models embed both images and text into the same vector space.\nThe original Sentence Transformers image-text models are based on CLIP. See Usage > Image Search for details on text-to-image search, image-to-image search, image clustering, and zero-shot image classification.\nThe following CLIP models are available with their respective Top 1 accuracy on zero-shot ImageNet validation dataset:\n| Model | Top 1 Performance |\n|---|---|\n| sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-L-14 | 75.4 |\n| sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-16 | 68.1 |\n| sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-32 | 63.3 |\nWe further provide this multilingual text-image model:",
    "character_count": 741
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fdd1dee1-1f3c-45c2-8eda-504273780594",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "text": "| sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-L-14 | 75.4 |\n| sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-16 | 68.1 |\n| sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-32 | 63.3 |\nWe further provide this multilingual text-image model:\n- sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-32-multilingual-v1 - Multilingual text encoder for the sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-32 model using Multilingual Knowledge Distillation. This model can encode text in 50+ languages to match the image vectors from the sentence-transformers/clip-ViT-B-32 model.\nNewer multimodal models use the unified Transformer module, which automatically detects supported modalities from the underlying model and processor. These models typically support richer input formats, including interleaved image-text inputs via chat messages. Notable examples include:",
    "character_count": 781
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ca8f6856-55fb-40b9-89f5-be5e3b12c7ae",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "text": "- Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Embedding-2B - A Qwen3-VL-based embedding model that supports text, image, and interleaved image-text inputs via message format. Useful for document screenshot embedding and cross-modal retrieval. See Training Examples > Multimodal for a finetuning example.\nVLM-based models support additional modalities and input formats compared to CLIP models. You can verify this with modalities:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Embedding-2B\")\nprint(model.modalities)\n# => ['text', 'image', 'video', 'message']\nThe \"message\" modality means the model accepts chat-style message inputs, allowing you to combine text and images in a single input. This is how VLM-based models handle interleaved multimodal content.\nAudio & Video Models",
    "character_count": 801
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f1eeb59d-1e69-462f-8419-f9518c1da20d",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
    "url": "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/pretrained_models.html",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/benchmark_pages.json",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "text": "Audio & Video Models\nThe Transformer module also supports audio and video modalities when the underlying model and processor provide them. Audio models accept file paths, numpy/torch arrays, dicts with \"array\" and \"sampling_rate\" keys, or torchcodec.AudioDecoder instances, while video models accept file paths, numpy/torch arrays, dicts with \"array\" and \"video_metadata\" keys, or torchcodec.VideoDecoder instances. As pretrained audio and video embedding models become available on the Hugging Face Hub, they can be loaded with SentenceTransformer just like any other model.\nINSTRUCTOR models\nSome INSTRUCTOR models, such as hkunlp/instructor-large, are natively supported in Sentence Transformers. These models are special, as they are trained with instructions in mind. Notably, the primary difference between normal Sentence Transformer models and Instructor models is that the latter do not include the instructions themselves in the pooling step.\nThe following models work out of the box:",
    "character_count": 994
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "9caad2ef-acd7-45d0-9000-16dda38b1faa",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "benchmark_pages",
