    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Releases: huggingface/sentence-transformers\nRelease list\nv5.6.1 - Flash Attention Fix for XLM-R and RoBERTa Models\nThis patch release fixes silently degraded embeddings for RoBERTa-family models when flash attention is requested with transformers v5, notably every XLM-R based multilingual embedding model (BAAI/bge-m3, intfloat/multilingual-e5-large, etc.). The bug affected v5.5.0, v5.5.1, and v5.6.0.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.6.1\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.6.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.6.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.6.1\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.6.1\n# Multimodal dependencies (optional):\npip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.6.1\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.6.1\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.6.1\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.6.1",
    "character_count": 985
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "444ec5e2-42bd-4c6f-a61a-70d0ecc6d4ad",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "pip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.6.1\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.6.1\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.6.1\nFix position_ids offsetting for RoBERTa-family models when flattening inputs (#3879)\nSince v5.5.0, the Transformer module flattens text-only batches into one packed sequence when flash attention is requested, skipping all padding overhead for a notable performance improvement. The position_ids of that packed sequence restart at 0 for every text, which is correct for the vast majority of models. RoBERTa-family architectures however compute positions as padding_idx + 1 + n for the n-th token, so every token read a position embedding shifted by padding_idx + 1 (usually 2). Nothing crashes, the embeddings are just silently worse.\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n# An affected configuration: flash attention with an XLM-R based model\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\n\"BAAI/bge-m3\",",
    "character_count": 981
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "252e5450-d5bc-46bf-83c9-6db1d6d44875",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n# An affected configuration: flash attention with an XLM-R based model\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\n\"BAAI/bge-m3\",\nmodel_kwargs={\"attn_implementation\": \"flash_attention_2\"},\n)\nMeasured on BAAI/bge-m3:\n| Evaluation | padded | packed, 0-based positions | packed, with this fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| stsb test Spearman | 0.8485 | 0.7239 | 0.8485 |\n| NanoBEIR mean nDCG@10 | 0.6041 | 0.5414 | 0.6050 |",
    "character_count": 451
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "12723d00-8a0d-4dad-a56c-f5aa6e3fe99c",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "| Evaluation | padded | packed, 0-based positions | packed, with this fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| stsb test Spearman | 0.8485 | 0.7239 | 0.8485 |\n| NanoBEIR mean nDCG@10 | 0.6041 | 0.5414 | 0.6050 |\nThe quality loss recovers exactly once the offset is applied. The fix scans the loaded model's modules once for an int padding_idx stored next to a learned position_embeddings table, and offsets the packed position_ids when that pair is found. An audit of transformers finds 16 architectures with that pair (roberta, xlm_roberta, xlm_roberta_xl, camembert, roberta_prelayernorm, xmod, data2vec_text, longformer, luke, ibert, mpnet, markuplm, lilt, layoutlmv3, esm, and pp_doclayout_v2), all offset by exactly padding_idx + 1, and no 0-based or rotary architecture matches.",
    "character_count": 769
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "504bcc0c-b4e6-4524-be33-0bb5efb655ba",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "You are only affected if you encoded text with flash attention requested on transformers v5 with a RoBERTa-family checkpoint. The default padded path (e.g. sdpa) was never affected, and neither were MPNet models like all-mpnet-base-v2 despite mpnet appearing in the audit: transformers does not support flash attention for MPNet at all. If you did index a corpus with such a configuration, re-encode it after upgrading: pre-fix embeddings score notably worse and do not mix with post-fix embeddings.\nWhat's Changed\n- [ci ] Exclude librosa/numba/llvmlite on Python 3.13 by @tomaarsen in #3835\n- [tests ] Skip bf16 + Windows + CPU forwards, as they can WindowsError on torch 2.13 by @tomaarsen in #3863\n- 🚨 Fix position_ids offsetting for RoBERTa-family models when flattening inputs by @tomaarsen in #3879\nFull Changelog: v5.6.0...v5.6.1\nv5.6.0 - Fixes for Causal LM Rerankers, Hard-Negative Mining, and More",
    "character_count": 907
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "273bfa88-31f2-47da-85a9-163f417ec61c",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "Full Changelog: v5.6.0...v5.6.1\nv5.6.0 - Fixes for Causal LM Rerankers, Hard-Negative Mining, and More\nThis minor version is a correctness- and robustness-focused release. It fixes a silent scoring bug for causal-LM rerankers, corrects several hard-negative mining and GIST loss edge cases, restores TSDAE on transformers v5, and adds Apple Silicon (MPS) support for the cached losses.\nThe headline fix affects chat-template models that read the final token position, i.e. causal-LM rerankers (like Qwen3-Reranker) and last-token-pooling embedders: when an over-long input was truncated, the chat template's trailing suffix (e.g. the assistant prefill the model scores from) was silently dropped, producing wrong scores with no error. There's also a forward-looking deprecation: loading local custom code without trust_remote_code=True now warns, and will require it from v6.0.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.6.0",
    "character_count": 974
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ac6d25de-663c-4946-951a-e8a28be06b9a",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "Install this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.6.0\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.6.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.6.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.6.0\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.6.0\n# Multimodal dependencies (optional):\npip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.6.0\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.6.0\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.6.0\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.6.0\nFixed silently wrong scores when truncation drops chat-template suffixes (#3787)",
    "character_count": 662
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a25930d8-89d2-48e4-9b43-99ae43993f53",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
