    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "text": "- Fix a reStructuredText table in the ContrastiveTensionLoss docstring in #3788, and add a low-VRAM hardware note to the efficiency docs in #3802.\n- Fix package build warnings and errors in #3809, and a batch of Sphinx doc-build problems in #3811.\nAll Changes\n- [chore ] Increment dev version by @tomaarsen in #3775\n- [fix ] Collapse single-key multimodal dicts to bare modality by @tomaarsen in #3779\n- chore: enable Dependabot weekly GitHub Actions bumps by @hf-dependantbot-rollout[bot] in #3786\n- Bump the actions group with 3 updates by @dependabot[bot] in #3790\n- Fix example datasets that crash on datasets 4.x by @omkar-334 in #3782\n- CLIP Notebooks Refresh by @lbourdois in #3780\n- fix TSDAE ...\nv5.5.1 - Small Multimodal patch\nThis patch release fixes a small quirk with multimodal inference when using single-key multimodal inputs like model.encode({\"image\": ...}).\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.5.1",
    "character_count": 973
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0b50be26-1818-4ad4-83eb-904b5de0c3f5",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "text": "Install this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.5.1\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.5.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.5.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.5.1\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.5.1\n# Multimodal dependencies (optional):\npip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.5.1\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.5.1\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.5.1\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.5.1\nBug fixed\nPreviously, inference like model.encode({\"image\": ...}) or model.encode([{\"image\": ...}, ...]) would be inferred as the (\"image\",) modality, which differed from the inferred modality of \"image\" for just model.encode(my_image) or model.encode([my_image, my_image_2, ...]).",
    "character_count": 863
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "15a1f806-046e-443b-94a8-0f18b68e4631",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "text": "This results in confusing errors if the model doesn't have a modality_config mapping for (\"image\",) in addition to \"image\", so now a single-key multimodal dict is collapsed to the bare modality (just \"image\" in this example).\nThis affected this code:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer('BAAI/BGE-VL-base', trust_remote_code=True)\nembedding = model.encode({\"image\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/blog/ettin-reranker/mteb_ndcg10_all-MiniLM-L6-v2.png\"})\nprint(embedding.shape)\nWhich previously failed as the model only implements a path for \"text\", \"image\", and (\"image\", \"text\").\nAll Changes\n- [fix] Collapse single-key multimodal dicts to bare modality by @tomaarsen in #3779\nFull Changelog: v5.5.0...v5.5.1\nv5.5.0 - Training Agent Skill, EmbedDistillLoss, and ADRMSELoss",
    "character_count": 866
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fb72c681-92bb-4639-866a-1ec76f1bc1b3",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "text": "All Changes\n- [fix] Collapse single-key multimodal dicts to bare modality by @tomaarsen in #3779\nFull Changelog: v5.5.0...v5.5.1\nv5.5.0 - Training Agent Skill, EmbedDistillLoss, and ADRMSELoss\nThis release ships the train-sentence-transformers Agent Skill, adds two new training losses, and brings a long list of robustness and correctness fixes.\nThe new train-sentence-transformers Agent Skill lets AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, ...) drive end-to-end training and fine-tuning across all three model types. EmbedDistillLoss is a new embedding-level knowledge distillation loss for SentenceTransformer: it aligns a student model's embeddings with pre-computed teacher embeddings, an alternative to the score-based distillation provided by MarginMSELoss and DistillKLDivLoss. ADRMSELoss is a new listwise learning-to-rank loss for CrossEncoder from the Rank-DistiLLM paper. encode() and predict() also gain a per-call processing_kwargs override, and more.",
    "character_count": 981
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d9c49ea7-58cf-4612-bbd0-d69d817ed11b",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "text": "Install this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.5.0\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.5.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.5.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.5.0\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.5.0\n# Multimodal dependencies (optional):\npip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.5.0\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.5.0\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.5.0\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.5.0\nThe train-sentence-transformers Agent Skill (#3752)\nIf you use an AI coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, ...), you can now install the train-sentence-transformers Agent Skill and ask your agent to fine-tune a model on your data:\nhf skills add train-sentence-transformers # installs under ./.agents/skills/",
    "character_count": 915
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "82c038bb-082f-4b1e-8021-25d39c3be5fa",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "text": "hf skills add train-sentence-transformers # installs under ./.agents/skills/\nhf skills add train-sentence-transformers --global # installs under ~/.agents/skills/\nhf skills add train-sentence-transformers --claude # also symlinks into .claude/skills/\nThe skill gives the agent curated, version-aware guidance for training SentenceTransformer (bi-encoder), CrossEncoder (reranker), and SparseEncoder/SPLADE models, covering base model selection, loss and evaluator choice, hard-negative mining, distillation, LoRA, Matryoshka, multilingual training, static embeddings, plus a set of production-ready training template scripts. Then you can prompt your agent with things like:\n\"Train a multilingual sentence-transformer on Dutch legal pairs.\"\n\"Fine-tune a cross-encoder reranker on (question, answer) pairs from my dataset, mine hard negatives, and push to my Hub repo.\"\n\"Train a German sparse embedding model with high sparsity.\"\n\"Can you train a static embedding model on 100k code triplets?\"",
    "character_count": 992
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "50e17d96-3058-4164-b25d-ca4f70fb855e",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "text": "\"Train a German sparse embedding model with high sparsity.\"\n\"Can you train a static embedding model on 100k code triplets?\"\nThe skill lives in the repository under skills/train-sentence-transformers/ and is mirrored to the huggingface/skills marketplace on each release.\nNew loss: EmbedDistillLoss (#3665)",
    "character_count": 305
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d22ea2ea-ba27-4bab-84a9-3e459161a99a",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "text": "New loss: EmbedDistillLoss (#3665)\nIntroduces EmbedDistillLoss (Kim et al., 2023), an embedding-level knowledge distillation loss for SentenceTransformer. Rather than distilling teacher scores (MarginMSELoss, DistillKLDivLoss), it directly aligns the student's sentence_embedding with a pre-computed teacher embedding passed via the dataset's label column. The comparison uses a configurable distance_metric, one of \"cosine\" (the default), \"l2\", or \"mse\". When the student and teacher dimensions differ, pass projection_dim=<teacher_dim> to add a learnable projection from the student's embedding space into the teacher's. That projection lives on the loss rather than on the saved model, so use loss.save_projection(...) / loss.load_projection(...) to reuse it across stages (e.g. like done in Arkam et al. for Jina v5). As part of this change, MSELoss is now a thin subclass of EmbedDistillLoss with distance_metric=\"mse\", and also gains the optional projection_dim argument.",
    "character_count": 977
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e4b9b34d-d9f8-4cd3-9b1f-774252f91acc",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "text": "from datasets import Dataset\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer, SentenceTransformerTrainer\nfrom sentence_transformers.sentence_transformer.losses import EmbedDistillLoss\nstudent_model = SentenceTransformer(\"microsoft/mpnet-base\")\nteacher_model = SentenceTransformer(\"all-mpnet-base-v2\")\ntrain_dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\n\"sentence\": [\"It's nice weather outside today.\", \"He drove to work.\"],\n})\n# Pre-compute teacher embeddings once and store them as the `label` column\ndef add_teacher_embeddings(batch):\nreturn {\"label\": teacher_model.encode(batch[\"sentence\"]).tolist()}\ntrain_dataset = train_dataset.map(add_teacher_embeddings, batched=True)\nloss = EmbedDistillLoss(student_model, distance_metric=\"cosine\")\n# If the student and teacher dimensions differ, add a learnable projection:\n# loss = EmbedDistillLoss(student_model, distance_metric=\"cosine\", projection_dim=768)\ntrainer = SentenceTransformerTrainer(\nmodel=student_model,\ntrain_dataset=train_dataset,\nloss=loss,\n)",
    "character_count": 994
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "495e718a-2267-46b9-b068-3640c584e1e2",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
