    "chunk_index": 26,
    "text": "# loss = EmbedDistillLoss(student_model, distance_metric=\"cosine\", projection_dim=768)\ntrainer = SentenceTransformerTrainer(\nmodel=student_model,\ntrain_dataset=train_dataset,\nloss=loss,\n)\ntrainer.train()\nSee the updated model distillation examples and the loss overview for more.\nNew loss: ADRMSELoss for Cross Encoders (#3690)\nIntroduces ADRMSELoss (Approx Discounted Rank Mean Squared Error), a listwise learning-to-rank loss for CrossEncoder from the Rank-DistiLLM paper (Schlatt et al., ECIR 2025). It computes a differentiable approximation of each document's rank via pairwise sigmoids and minimizes the nDCG-discounted squared error against the true ranks derived from the labels. It expects listwise inputs: a (query, [doc1, ..., docN]) pair plus a [score1, ..., scoreN] label list per sample (binary or continuous labels, variable document counts allowed). It's designed for LLM-distillation reranking, where the per-document scores come from a strong LLM's ordering.",
    "character_count": 976
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d026907e-72c1-48b8-9e69-ec4ae4d09908",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "text": "from datasets import Dataset\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder, CrossEncoderTrainer\nfrom sentence_transformers.cross_encoder.losses import ADRMSELoss\nmodel = CrossEncoder(\"microsoft/mpnet-base\")\ntrain_dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\n\"query\": [\"What are pandas?\", \"What is the capital of France?\"],\n\"docs\": [\n[\"Pandas are a kind of bear.\", \"Pandas are kind of like fish.\"],\n[\"The capital of France is Paris.\", \"Paris is the capital of France.\", \"Paris is quite large.\"],\n],\n\"scores\": [[0.95, 0.1], [0.98, 0.92, 0.2]],\n})\nloss = ADRMSELoss(model)\ntrainer = CrossEncoderTrainer(\nmodel=model,\ntrain_dataset=train_dataset,\nloss=loss,\n)\ntrainer.train()\nThere's a full MS MARCO example at training_ms_marco_adrmse.py. Note that LambdaLoss generally remains the strongest loss in the listwise family. See the Cross Encoder loss overview for guidance on picking a loss.\nPer-call processing_kwargs override (#3753)",
    "character_count": 915
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a56f302f-578d-4536-bd2b-480c9102b1dd",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "text": "Per-call processing_kwargs override (#3753)\nSentenceTransformer.encode() / encode_query() / encode_document(), SparseEncoder.encode(), CrossEncoder.predict(), and model.preprocess() now accept a processing_kwargs argument that overrides the processor/tokenizer kwargs configured at construction time, for a single call. It has the same nested structure as the processing_kwargs constructor argument (top-level keys text, audio, image, video, common, chat_template) and is shallow-merged on top of the instance-level settings, so you can override just one setting (e.g. max_length) and leave the rest intact.\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")\n# Override processor kwargs (e.g. max_length, truncation) for this call only:\nembeddings = model.encode(\n[\"a short text\", \"a much longer text that you want truncated more aggressively ...\"],\nprocessing_kwargs={\"text\": {\"max_length\": 256, \"truncation\": True}},\n)",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "385dabb1-1b49-44b2-a421-f92e0eb55043",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
