    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "text": "embeddings = model.encode(\n[\"a short text\", \"a much longer text that you want truncated more aggressively ...\"],\nprocessing_kwargs={\"text\": {\"max_length\": 256, \"truncation\": True}},\n)\nThis is especially handy for vision-language models, where you can change the image resolution per call, e.g. model.encode(images, processing_kwargs={\"image\": {\"max_pixels\": 256 * 256}}).\nSmaller Features\n- Allow CrossEncoder module stacks that don't start with aTransformer , and recognize a trailingDense(module_output_name=\"scores\") as the scoring head, by @tomaarsen in #3742:num_labels now reads that head'sout_features , andmodel.config /model.model returnNone when there's no underlying transformers model.",
    "character_count": 697
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f4a9d773-2e32-43d5-8120-fa743584dca0",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
