    "chunk_index": 30,
    "text": "- Infer that a model is an IR model on its generated model card when an InformationRetrievalEvaluator /NanoBEIREvaluator (or their sparse variants) was used during training, by @tomaarsen in #3741: the usage snippet then showsencode_query /encode_document , even without IR prompt names or aRouter architecture.\n- Warn at model-load time when the installed transformers version is too old to honoruse_bidirectional_attention /is_causal flags in a model's config (e.g. forgoogle/embeddinggemma-300m ), rather than silently ignoring them, by @tomaarsen in #3726.\nBug Fixes\n- Use the first non-pad token for CLS pooling with left-padding tokenizers by @tomaarsen in #3767: pooling_mode=\"cls\" previously returned the embedding at position 0, which is a[PAD] token for left-padded inputs (common with decoder-only models), silently producing incorrect sentence embeddings. It now ...\nv5.4.1 - Numpy string arrays",
    "character_count": 907
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "74215e14-bd6d-4cf8-a808-98d2a5ea8cb9",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
