    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "text": "v5.4.1 - Numpy string arrays\nThis patch release allows encode() and predict() to accept 1D numpy string arrays as inputs.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.4.1\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.4.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.4.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.4.1\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.4.1\n# Multimodal dependencies (optional):\npip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.4.1\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.4.1\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.4.1\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.4.1\nNumpy string/object arrays as batches (#3720)",
    "character_count": 749
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "30e8378b-ffca-4fb6-8d9a-a55f9b23748f",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "text": "pip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.4.1\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.4.1\nNumpy string/object arrays as batches (#3720)\nencode() and predict() now correctly recognize 1D numpy string/object arrays as batches rather than singular inputs. Previously, something like model.encode(df[\"text\"].to_numpy()) was silently treated as a single input and produced incorrect output. 1D numpy arrays with dtype.kind in (\"U\", \"O\") are now unpacked like lists, and 2D+ arrays are treated as batches of pairs (for CrossEncoder).\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")\n# Previously treated as one input; now correctly encoded as 3 separate texts\nembeddings = model.encode(np.array([\"first\", \"second\", \"third\"]))\nprint(embeddings.shape)\n# (3, 384)",
    "character_count": 867
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b860e13d-3f71-4630-9568-67313f179a80",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 33,
    "text": "# Previously treated as one input; now correctly encoded as 3 separate texts\nembeddings = model.encode(np.array([\"first\", \"second\", \"third\"]))\nprint(embeddings.shape)\n# (3, 384)\nFor CrossEncoder, a 1D numpy string array is still treated as a single [query, document] pair to match the existing list behavior, while a 2D array of shape (N, 2) is a batch of N pairs.\nSafer activation function loading in Dense (#3714)\nThe Dense module stores its activation function as a dotted import path in its saved config (e.g. \"torch.nn.modules.activation.Tanh\"), which was then resolved via import_from_string whenever the module was loaded. Because any importable Python callable could be referenced, a maliciously crafted config.json on the Hub could trigger arbitrary imports at model load time.",
    "character_count": 786
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "02298f11-dbf3-4de8-aa8f-177c53d7bcae",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 34,
    "text": "The loader now only resolves activation functions whose import path starts with torch.. Anything else is skipped with a warning and replaced by the default activation (Tanh). To load a model with a custom (non-torch) activation function, opt in explicitly with trust_remote_code=True:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n# Torch-provided activations load as before\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"some/model-with-torch-activation\")\n# Non-torch activations now require explicit opt-in\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"some/model-with-custom-activation\", trust_remote_code=True)\nThis mirrors the opt-in trust model already used by transformers for custom code, and ensures untrusted model repositories cannot smuggle arbitrary imports through the Dense activation config.\nWhat's Changed\n- [tests ] Fix test_trainer_prompts for SE and ST after prompt handling moved into Transformer.preprocess by @tomaarsen in #3710\n- [chore ] Increment dev version after v5.4 release by @tomaarsen in #3711",
    "character_count": 999
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "858db366-3a5d-48db-9948-1f17c43b4231",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 35,
    "text": "- [chore ] Increment dev version after v5.4 release by @tomaarsen in #3711\n- [docs ] No revision needed anymore for nvidia nemotron by @tomaarsen in #3712\n- [chore ] Replace evaluation_strategy with eval_strategy in a few more places by @tomaarsen in #3713\n- [security ] Only load activation functions starting with 'torch' in the Dense module by @tomaarsen in #3714\n- [fix ] Treat numpy string/object arrays as batches in encode/predict by @tomaarsen in #3720\nFull Changelog: v5.4.0...v5.4.1\nv5.4.0 - Multimodal Embeddings and Reranking, Modular CrossEncoder, Flash Attention Input Flattening",
    "character_count": 593
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8592b4d1-51da-4c13-858b-b53dc0c88072",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 36,
    "text": "Full Changelog: v5.4.0...v5.4.1\nv5.4.0 - Multimodal Embeddings and Reranking, Modular CrossEncoder, Flash Attention Input Flattening\nThis large release introduces first-class multimodal support for both SentenceTransformer and CrossEncoder, making it easy to compute embeddings and rerank across text, images, audio, and video. The CrossEncoder class has been fully modularized, allowing for generative rerankers (CausalLM-based models) via a new LogitScore module. Flash Attention 2 now automatically skips padding for text-only inputs, providing significant speedups & memory reductions, especially when input lengths vary.\nBlog post: Multimodal Embedding & Reranker Models with Sentence Transformers: a walkthrough of the new multimodal capabilities with some practical examples.",
    "character_count": 782
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0fc2332b-69a3-47a0-b4c7-7685368b7b57",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 37,
    "text": "Blog post: Multimodal Embedding & Reranker Models with Sentence Transformers: a walkthrough of the new multimodal capabilities with some practical examples.\nMigration guide: Migrating from v5.x to v5.4+: covers updated import paths, renamed parameters, and other softly breaking changes with deprecation warnings. Note that there are no hard deprecations, all existing code should continue to work with warnings at worst.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.4.0\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.4.0\n# Multimodal dependencies (optional):\npip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.4.0\n# Or combine as needed:",
    "character_count": 944
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "63b8f0b5-95a7-475b-b3b1-a3c44642970b",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 38,
    "text": "pip install sentence-transformers[image]==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[audio]==5.4.0\npip install sentence-transformers[video]==5.4.0\n# Or combine as needed:\npip install sentence-transformers[train,onnx,image]==5.4.0\nMultimodal Embeddings with SentenceTransformer (#3554)\nSentenceTransformer now natively supports vision-language models (VLMs) and other multimodal architectures. You can encode and compare across text, images, audio, videos, or combinations of these, with automatic modality detection and preprocessing. Models advertise which modalities they support via the new model.modalities property and model.supports() method.\nUsing a pretrained multimodal embedding model\nfrom PIL import Image\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\n\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Embedding-2B\",\nmodel_kwargs={\"attn_implementation\": \"flash_attention_2\", \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\"},\nprocessor_kwargs={\"min_pixels\": 28 * 28, \"max_pixels\": 600 * 600},",
    "character_count": 979
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "32f6d9ce-3469-4e33-899a-6ef766c92ccd",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 39,
    "text": "\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Embedding-2B\",\nmodel_kwargs={\"attn_implementation\": \"flash_attention_2\", \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\"},\nprocessor_kwargs={\"min_pixels\": 28 * 28, \"max_pixels\": 600 * 600},\nrevision=\"refs/pr/23\",\n)\n# Check supported modalities\nprint(model.modalities)\n# ['text', 'image', 'video', 'message']\nprint(model.supports(\"image\"))\n# True\n# Encode text\ntext_embeddings = model.encode([\"A photo of a cat\", \"A pollinator on a flower\"])\n# Encode images (PIL images, file paths, or URLs all work)\nimage_embeddings = model.encode([\nImage.open(\"cat.jpg\"),\n\"https://example.com/flower.jpg\",\n])\n# Encode mixed text+image inputs\nmultimodal_embeddings = model.encode([\n{\"text\": \"Describe this image\", \"image\": Image.open(\"cat.jpg\")},\n])\n# Compute cross-modal similarity\nsimilarity = model.similarity(text_embeddings, image_embeddings)\nBuilding multimodal models with Router",
    "character_count": 863
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "284eb16c-73dc-4ccc-b5d4-3c38b4275f54",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 40,
    "text": "])\n# Compute cross-modal similarity\nsimilarity = model.similarity(text_embeddings, image_embeddings)\nBuilding multimodal models with Router\nYou can also compose separate encoders for different modalities using the new Router module. Unlike the single-backbone VLM approach, Router lets you combine any existing text and image encoders and route inputs based on detected modality:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nfrom sentence_transformers.sentence_transformer.modules import Dense, Pooling, Router, Transformer\n# Text encoder: MiniLM with mean pooling, projected to 768 dims to match image encoder\ntext_encoder = Transformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")\ntext_pooling = Pooling(text_encoder.get_embedding_dimension(), pooling_mode=\"mean\")\ntext_projection = Dense(text_encoder.get_embedding_dimension(), 768)\n# Image encoder: SigLIP outputs pooled embeddings directly\nimage_encoder = Transformer(\"google/siglip2-base-patch16-224\")",
    "character_count": 963
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3cf2c486-9b0a-4488-a3a6-d1e71cba523e",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "text": "text_projection = Dense(text_encoder.get_embedding_dimension(), 768)\n# Image encoder: SigLIP outputs pooled embeddings directly\nimage_encoder = Transformer(\"google/siglip2-base-patch16-224\")\n# Route inputs to the appropriate encoder based on detected modality\nrouter = Router(\nsub_modules={\n\"text\": [text_encoder, text_pooling, text_projection],\n\"image\": [image_encoder],\n},\n)\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(modules=[router])\n# Text and image inputs are automatically routed to the correct encoder\ntext_embeddings = model.encode([\"A photo of a cat\"])\nimage_embeddings = model.encode([\"https://example.com/cat.jpg\"])\nsimilarity = model.similarity(text_embeddings, image_embeddings)\nMultimodal Reranking with CrossEncoder (#3554)",
    "character_count": 724
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "17e50d8f-1594-4a3d-ba40-bd1d89354bd2",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 42,
    "text": "image_embeddings = model.encode([\"https://example.com/cat.jpg\"])\nsimilarity = model.similarity(text_embeddings, image_embeddings)\nMultimodal Reranking with CrossEncoder (#3554)\nCrossEncoder now supports multimodal inputs for reranking, enabling cross-modal scoring of query-document pairs where either side can be text, images, audio, video, or mixed-modality content. This works with both generative rerankers (CausalLM-based, via the new LogitScore module) and encoder-based models. See the pretrained multimodal rerankers for models you can use right away.\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\n# Load a multimodal reranker\nmodel = CrossEncoder(\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Reranker-2B\", revision=\"refs/pr/11\")\n# Rank text documents against an image query (or vice versa)\nresults = model.rank(\nquery=\"https://example.com/product.jpg\",\ndocuments=[\"A red sneaker\", \"A blue dress\", \"A leather bag\"],\n)\nTwo training approaches are provided in the multimodal training examples:",
    "character_count": 970
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ef48c4c6-3fed-4c26-b9ce-1f609ec963ee",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 43,
    "text": "query=\"https://example.com/product.jpg\",\ndocuments=[\"A red sneaker\", \"A blue dress\", \"A leather bag\"],\n)\nTwo training approaches are provided in the multimodal training examples:\n- Any-to-Any + LogitScore: Uses the full causal LM to generate a single token, scoring via log-odds of \"1\" vs \"0\".\n- Feature Extraction + Pooling + Dense: More memory-efficient alternative that skips the LM head.\nModular CrossEncoder Architecture (#3554)\nCrossEncoder has been fully modularized, inheriting from BaseModel (which is a torch.nn.Sequential). You can now inspect, customize, and compose module chains, just like SentenceTransformer. See the custom models guide for full details.\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\nmodel = CrossEncoder(\"Qwen/Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B\", revision=\"refs/pr/11\")\nprint(model)\n\"\"\"\nCrossEncoder(\n(0): Transformer({'transformer_task': 'text-generation', ...})\n(1): LogitScore({'true_token_id': 9693, 'false_token_id': 2152, ...})\n)\n\"\"\"\nGenerative reranker support",
    "character_count": 987
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "adba6033-b9c9-4f40-a3da-03b3fdb0ef20",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
