    "chunk_index": 44,
    "text": "print(model)\n\"\"\"\nCrossEncoder(\n(0): Transformer({'transformer_task': 'text-generation', ...})\n(1): LogitScore({'true_token_id': 9693, 'false_token_id': 2152, ...})\n)\n\"\"\"\nGenerative reranker support\nThanks to the modular architecture, generative rerankers like mixedbread-ai/mxbai-rerank-base-v2 now work out of the box. These models ship with a modules.json that configures the Transformer + LogitScore chain automatically:\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\nmodel = CrossEncoder(\"mixedbread-ai/mxbai-rerank-base-v2\")\nscores = model.predict([\n(\"How many people live in Berlin?\", \"Berlin had a population of 3,520,031 in 2022.\"),\n(\"How many people live in Berlin?\", \"Berlin is well known for its museums.\"),\n])\n# array([ 9. , -0.5], dtype=float32)\nModule chain patterns\nThe Transformer module now supports multiple task types that determine how the underlying model is loaded and what outputs it produces:",
    "character_count": 916
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "245a0e96-2770-4c1e-bd8f-6805a44bf347",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 45,
    "text": "])\n# array([ 9. , -0.5], dtype=float32)\nModule chain patterns\nThe Transformer module now supports multiple task types that determine how the underlying model is loaded and what outputs it produces:\n- \"sequence-classification\" : Loads viaAutoModelForSequenceClassification , returns classification logits directly.\n- \"text-generation\" : Loads viaAutoModelForCausalLM , returns raw logits from the language model head.\n- \"any-to-any\" : Loads viaAutoModelForMultimodalLM (transformers v5+), for multimodal causal LMs that accept interleaved image/text inputs.\n- \"feature-extraction\" : Loads viaAutoModel (no task-specific head), returns hidden states.\nVarious module chains are possible now, here's some common ones:\n-\nEncoder-based (Sequence Classification): A single Transformer module withtransformer_task=\"sequence-classification\" , the traditional BERT/RoBERTa approach. This was previously the only option for CrossEncoder models.\n-",
    "character_count": 935
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "6826a3a6-5241-45f4-bd99-fde284310df3",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 46,
    "text": "-\nCausalLM-based (Text Generation + LogitScore): For generative rerankers (Qwen, Llama, mxbai-rerank-v2, etc.), a Transformer withtransformer_task=\"text-generation\" followed by aLogitScore module that computeslogit[\"yes\"] - logit[\"no\"] at the last token position. For multimodal rerankers,transformer_task=\"any-to-any\" is used instead.\n-\nFeature Extraction + Pooling + Dense: A memory-efficient alternative that uses the base model without LM head, pools the last token, and projects to a single score via a Dense layer.\nWhen loading a model without a modules.json, CrossEncoder automatically selects the right chain: if the architecture ends with ForCausalLM, it uses text-generation + LogitScore (with \"yes\"/\"no\" tokens); otherwise it uses sequence-classification. You can also construct custom module chains explicitly:\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\nfrom sentence_transformers.cross_encoder.modules import Transformer, LogitScore",
    "character_count": 949
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "6388fdb6-6fa5-4ef5-b4b8-8688c0bdf154",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 47,
    "text": "from sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\nfrom sentence_transformers.cross_encoder.modules import Transformer, LogitScore\ntransformer = Transformer(\"Qwen/Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B\", transformer_task=\"text-generation\", revision=\"refs/pr/11\")\ntrue_id = transformer.tokenizer.convert_tokens_to_ids(\"1\")...\nv5.3.0 - Improved Contrastive Learning, New Losses, and Transformers v5 Compatibility\nThis minor version brings several improvements to contrastive learning: MultipleNegativesRankingLoss now supports alternative InfoNCE formulations (symmetric, GTE-style) and optional hardness weighting for harder negatives. Two new losses are introduced, GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss for embedding space regularization and CachedSpladeLoss for memory-efficient SPLADE training. The release also adds a faster hashed batch sampler, fixes GroupByLabelBatchSampler for triplet losses, and ensures full compatibility with the latest Transformers v5 versions.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference",
    "character_count": 997
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "be74f276-8adf-4cc5-a333-ea80f7b8ba74",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 48,
    "text": "Install this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.3.0\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.3.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.3.0\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.3.0\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.3.0\nUpdated MultipleNegativesRankingLoss (a.k.a. InfoNCE)\nMultipleNegativesRankingLoss received two major upgrades: support for alternative InfoNCE formulations from the literature, and optional hardness weighting to up-weight harder negatives.\nSupport other InfoNCE variants (#3607)\nMultipleNegativesRankingLoss now supports several well-known contrastive loss variants from the literature through new directions and partition_mode parameters. Previously, this loss only supported the standard forward direction (query → doc). You can now configure which similarity interactions are included in the loss:",
    "character_count": 918
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c98461f7-9f7d-44db-aea1-ec04c0755ab4",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 49,
    "text": "- \"query_to_doc\" (default): For each query, its matched document should score higher than all other documents.\n- \"doc_to_query\" : The symmetric reverse — for each document, its matched query should score higher than all other queries.\n- \"query_to_query\" : For each query, all other queries should score lower than its matched document.\n- \"doc_to_doc\" : For each document, all other documents should score lower than its matched query.\nThe partition_mode controls how scores are normalized: \"joint\" computes a single softmax over all directions, while \"per_direction\" computes a separate softmax per direction and averages the losses.\nThese combine to reproduce several loss formulations from the literature:\nStandard InfoNCE (default, unchanged behavior):\nloss = MultipleNegativesRankingLoss(model)\n# equivalent to directions=(\"query_to_doc\",), partition_mode=\"joint\"\nSymmetric InfoNCE (Günther et al. 2024) — adds the reverse direction so both queries and documents are trained to find their match:",
    "character_count": 999
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d8821906-b4c1-411f-bc44-f3de0f538bb5",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 50,
    "text": "Symmetric InfoNCE (Günther et al. 2024) — adds the reverse direction so both queries and documents are trained to find their match:\nloss = MultipleNegativesRankingLoss(\nmodel,\ndirections=(\"query_to_doc\", \"doc_to_query\"),\npartition_mode=\"per_direction\",\n)\nGTE improved contrastive loss (Li et al. 2023) — adds same-type negatives (query <-> query, doc <-> doc) for a stronger training signal, especially useful with pairs-only data:\nloss = MultipleNegativesRankingLoss(\nmodel,\ndirections=(\"query_to_doc\", \"query_to_query\", \"doc_to_query\", \"doc_to_doc\"),\npartition_mode=\"joint\",\n)\nHardness-weighted contrastive learning (#3667)\nAdds optional hardness weighting to MultipleNegativesRankingLoss and CachedMultipleNegativesRankingLoss, inspired by Lan et al. 2025 (LLaVE). This up-weights harder negatives in the softmax by adding hardness_strength * stop_grad(cos_sim) to selected negative logits. The feature is off by default (hardness_mode=None), so existing behavior is unchanged.",
    "character_count": 980
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "62faf81d-9109-4e9b-a4de-39a44ced9d96",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 51,
    "text": "The hardness_mode parameter controls which negatives receive the penalty:\n- \"in_batch_negatives\" : Penalizes in-batch negatives only (positives and hard negatives from other samples). Works with all data formats including pairs-only.\n- \"hard_negatives\" : Penalizes explicit hard negatives only (columns beyond the first two). Only active when hard negatives are provided.\n- \"all_negatives\" : Penalizes both in-batch and hard negatives, leaving only the positive unpenalized.\nfrom sentence_transformers.losses import MultipleNegativesRankingLoss\nloss = MultipleNegativesRankingLoss(\nmodel,\nhardness_mode=\"in_batch_negatives\",\nhardness_strength=9.0,\n)\nNew loss: GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss (#3654)",
    "character_count": 702
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "18933805-571f-407c-9e89-774e1c0481a5",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 52,
    "text": "loss = MultipleNegativesRankingLoss(\nmodel,\nhardness_mode=\"in_batch_negatives\",\nhardness_strength=9.0,\n)\nNew loss: GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss (#3654)\nIntroduces GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss (Zhang et al. 2017), a regularization loss that encourages embeddings to be well-distributed in the embedding space. It penalizes two things: (1) high mean pairwise similarity across unrelated embeddings, and (2) high second moment of similarities (which indicates clustering). This loss is meant to be combined with a primary contrastive loss like MultipleNegativesRankingLoss. By wrapping both losses in a single module, you can share embeddings and only require one forward pass:\nimport torch\nfrom datasets import Dataset\nfrom torch import Tensor\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer, SentenceTransformerTrainer\nfrom sentence_transformers.losses import GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss, MultipleNegativesRankingLoss\nfrom sentence_transformers.util import cos_sim",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "99ac55dc-5904-4278-b61b-08371a2ec845",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 53,
    "text": "from sentence_transformers.losses import GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss, MultipleNegativesRankingLoss\nfrom sentence_transformers.util import cos_sim\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"microsoft/mpnet-base\")\ntrain_dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\n\"anchor\": [\"It's nice weather outside today.\", \"He drove to work.\"],\n\"positive\": [\"It's so sunny.\", \"He took the car to the office.\"],\n})\nclass InfoNCEGORLoss(torch.nn.Module):\ndef __init__(self, model: SentenceTransformer, similarity_fct=cos_sim, scale=20.0) -> None:\nsuper().__init__()\nself.model = model\nself.info_nce_loss = MultipleNegativesRankingLoss(model, similarity_fct=similarity_fct, scale=scale)\nself.gor_loss = GlobalOrthogonalRegularizationLoss(model, similarity_fct=similarity_fct)\ndef forward(self, sentence_features: list[dict[str, Tensor]], labels: Tensor | None = None) -> Tensor:\nembeddings = [self.model(sentence_feature)[\"sentence_embedding\"] for sentence_feature in sentence_features]\ninfo_nce_loss: dict[str, Tensor] = {",
    "character_count": 985
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "57254068-4131-4aa8-92d9-8f6ef785c589",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 54,
    "text": "embeddings = [self.model(sentence_feature)[\"sentence_embedding\"] for sentence_feature in sentence_features]\ninfo_nce_loss: dict[str, Tensor] = {\n\"info_nce\": self.info_nce_loss.compute_loss_from_embeddings(embeddings, labels)\n}\ngor_loss: dict[str, Tensor] = self.gor_loss.compute_loss_from_embeddings(embeddings, labels)\nreturn {**info_nce_loss, **gor_loss}\nloss = InfoNCEGORLoss(model)\ntrainer = SentenceTransformerTrainer(\nmodel=model,\ntrain_dataset=train_dataset,\nloss=loss,\n)\ntrainer.train()\nNew loss: CachedSpladeLoss for memory-efficient SPLADE training (#3670)\nIntroduces CachedSpladeLoss, a gradient-cached version of SpladeLoss that enables training SPLADE models with larger batch sizes without additional GPU memory. It applies the GradCache technique at the SpladeLoss wrapper level, so both the base loss and regularizers receive pre-computed embeddings — no changes to existing base losses or regularizers are needed.\nfrom datasets import Dataset",
    "character_count": 959
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "297ca5f0-abda-4334-ba8c-720108ba950a",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 55,
    "text": "from datasets import Dataset\nfrom sentence_transformers.sparse_encoder import SparseEncoder, SparseEncoderTrainer\nfrom sentence_transformers.sparse_encoder.losses import CachedSpladeLoss, SparseMultipleNegativesRankingLoss\nmodel = SparseEncoder(\"distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased\")\ntrain_dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\n\"anchor\": [\"It's nice weather outside today.\", \"He drove to work.\"],\n\"positive\": [\"It's so sunny.\", \"He took the car to the office.\"],\n})\nloss = CachedSpladeLoss(\nmodel=model,\nloss=SparseMultipleNegativesRankingLoss(model),\ndocument_regularizer_weight=3e-5,\nquery_regularizer_weight=5e-5,\nmini_batch_size=32,\n)\ntrainer = SparseEncoderTrainer(model=model, train_dataset=train_dataset, loss=loss)\ntrainer.train()\nFaster NoDuplicatesBatchSampler with hashing (#3611)",
    "character_count": 782
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8e207253-b7cd-42dd-8889-e088061a2fb2",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 56,
    "text": "mini_batch_size=32,\n)\ntrainer = SparseEncoderTrainer(model=model, train_dataset=train_dataset, loss=loss)\ntrainer.train()\nFaster NoDuplicatesBatchSampler with hashing (#3611)\nAdds a NO_DUPLICATES_HASHED batch sampler option, which uses the existing NoDuplicatesBatchSampler with precompute_hashes=True. This pre-computes xxhash 64-bit values for each sample, providing significant speedups for large batch sizes at a small memory cost. Requires the xxhash library.\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformerTrainingArguments\nargs = SentenceTransformerTrainingArguments(\nbatch_sampler=\"NO_DUPLICATES_HASHED\" # Pre-computes hashes for faster duplicate checking\n)\nGroupByLabelBatchSampler improvements for triplet losses (#3668)",
    "character_count": 736
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "6cc691c3-5acd-4d4b-aa09-730db933f9de",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 57,
    "text": "batch_sampler=\"NO_DUPLICATES_HASHED\" # Pre-computes hashes for faster duplicate checking\n)\nGroupByLabelBatchSampler improvements for triplet losses (#3668)\nFixes a critical issue where GroupByLabelBatchSampler produced ~99% single-class batches, causing zero gradients with triplet losses. The sampler now uses round-robin interleaving where each label emits 2 samples per round, with the label visit order reshuffled every round. This guarantees every batch contains multiple distinct labels, each with at least 2 samples.\nTransformers v5 compatibility\nThis release includes full compatibility updates for Transformers v5:\n- Compatibility with transformers 5.0.0rc01 and later versions (#3597, #3615)\n- Support for T5Gemma and T5Gemma2 models (#3644)\n- Transformers v5.2 compatibility for the trainer's _nested_gather method (#3664)\n- Support for both warmup_steps andwarmup_ratio until Transformers v4 support is dropped (#3645)\n- Updated CI to test against full Transformers v5 (#3615)",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d4bb8e90-6182-4d5f-af95-07babe5ed795",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 58,
    "text": "- Support for both warmup_steps andwarmup_ratio until Transformers v4 support is dropped (#3645)\n- Updated CI to test against full Transformers v5 (#3615)\nMinor Features\n- Add triplets/n-tuple support to AnglE by @tomaarsen in #3609\n- Replace requests dependency with optionalhttpx dependency by @tomaarsen in #3618\n- Specify numpy manually in dependencies by @tomaarsen in #3608\n- Support excluding prompt tokens with pooling with left-padding tokenizer by @tomaarsen in #3598\nBug Fixes\nv5.2.3 - Compatibility with Transformers v5.2 training\nThis patch release introduces compatibility with Transformers v5.2.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.2.3\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.2.3\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.2.3\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.2.3\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.2.3\nTransformers v5.2 Support",
    "character_count": 953
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "61592633-d9a1-4f8f-833c-985a8edd4f30",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 59,
    "text": "pip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.2.3\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.2.3\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.2.3\nTransformers v5.2 Support\nTransformers v5.2 has just released, and it updated its Trainer in such a way that training with Sentence Transformers would start failing on the logging step. The #3664 pull request has resolved this issue.\nIf you're not training with Sentence Transformers, then older versions of Sentence Transformers are also compatible with Transformers v5.2.\nAll Changes\n- [compat ] Introduce Transformers v5.2 compatibility: trainer _nested_gather moved by @tomaarsen (#3664)\nFull Changelog: v5.2.2...v5.2.3\nv5.2.2 - Replace mandatory `requests` dependency with optional `httpx` dependency\nThis patch release replaces mandatory requests dependency with an optional httpx dependency.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.2.2\n# Inference only, use one of:",
    "character_count": 974
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f0a8e20a-3cdc-48ce-8edb-db21dca9be2f",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 60,
    "text": "Install this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.2.2\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.2.2\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.2.2\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.2.2\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.2.2\nTransformers v5 Support\nTransformers v5.0 and its required huggingface_hub versions have dropped support of requests in favor of httpx. The former was also used in sentence-transformers, but not listed explicitly as a dependency. This patch removes the use of requests in favor of httpx, although it's now optional and not automatically imported. This should also save some import time.\nImporting Sentence Transformers should now not crash if requests is not installed.\nAll Changes\n- [deps ] Replace requests dependency with optional httpx dependency by @tomaarsen (#3618)\nFull Changelog: v5.2.1...v5.2.2\nv5.2.1 - Joint Transformers v4 and v5 compatibility",
    "character_count": 973
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "94040f49-d949-4bd5-8a39-44e1c0811f3e",
    "technology": "Sentence Transformers",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-transformers",
    "category": "embeddings",
    "organization": "UKPLab",
    "license": "Apache 2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "url": "https://github.com/UKPLab/sentence-transformers/releases",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/release_notes.json",
    "chunk_index": 61,
    "text": "All Changes\n- [deps ] Replace requests dependency with optional httpx dependency by @tomaarsen (#3618)\nFull Changelog: v5.2.1...v5.2.2\nv5.2.1 - Joint Transformers v4 and v5 compatibility\nThis patch release adds support for the full Transformers v5 release.\nInstall this version with\n# Training + Inference\npip install sentence-transformers[train]==5.2.1\n# Inference only, use one of:\npip install sentence-transformers==5.2.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx-gpu]==5.2.1\npip install sentence-transformers[onnx]==5.2.1\npip install sentence-transformers[openvino]==5.2.1\nTransformers v5 Support",
    "character_count": 597
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d57ff286-f1fd-4200-a554-a8cfce305842",
