    "path": "sentence_based_chunking/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "LlamaIndex OSS (by LlamaIndex) is an open-source framework to build agentic applications. Parse is our enterprise platform for agentic OCR, parsing, extraction, indexing and more. You can use LlamaParse with this framework or on its own; see LlamaParse below for signup and product links.\nBuilding with LlamaIndex typically involves working with LlamaIndex core and a chosen set of integrations (or plugins). There are two ways to start building with LlamaIndex in Python:\n-\nStarter: llama-index . A starter Python package that includes core LlamaIndex as well as a selection of integrations.\n-\nCustomized: llama-index-core . Install core LlamaIndex and add your chosen LlamaIndex integration packages on LlamaHub\nthat are required for your application. There are over 300 LlamaIndex integration\npackages that work seamlessly with core, allowing you to build with your preferred\nLLM, embedding, and vector store providers.\nThe LlamaIndex Python library is namespaced such that import statements which",
    "character_count": 1000
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c79ee2f0-f713-45fc-bce0-d1a78c0a336e",
    "technology": "Sentence-Based Chunking",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-based-chunking",
    "category": "chunking",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/run-llama/llama_index",
    "path": "sentence_based_chunking/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "LLM, embedding, and vector store providers.\nThe LlamaIndex Python library is namespaced such that import statements which\ninclude core imply that the core package is being used. In contrast, those\nstatements without core imply that an integration package is being used.\n# typical pattern\nfrom llama_index.core.xxx import ClassABC # core submodule xxx\nfrom llama_index.xxx.yyy import (\nSubclassABC,\n) # integration yyy for submodule xxx\n# concrete example\nfrom llama_index.core.llms import LLM\nfrom llama_index.llms.openai import OpenAI\nLlamaParse is its own platform—focused on document agents and agentic OCR. It includes Parse (parsing), LlamaAgents (deployed document agents), Extract (structured extraction), and Index (ingest and RAG). You can use it with the LlamaIndex framework or standalone.\n- Sign up for LlamaParse — Create an account and get your API key.\n- Parse — Agentic OCR and document parsing (130+ formats). Docs\n- Extract — Structured data extraction from documents. Docs",
    "character_count": 991
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0c77b22d-81a8-44e9-9739-3cbfe86d9055",
    "technology": "Sentence-Based Chunking",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-based-chunking",
    "category": "chunking",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/run-llama/llama_index",
    "path": "sentence_based_chunking/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "- Sign up for LlamaParse — Create an account and get your API key.\n- Parse — Agentic OCR and document parsing (130+ formats). Docs\n- Extract — Structured data extraction from documents. Docs\n- Index — Ingest, index, and RAG pipelines. Docs\n- Split — Split large documents into subcategories. Docs\n- Agents — Build end-to-end document agents with Workflows and Agent Builder. Docs\nNOTE: This README is not updated as frequently as the documentation. Please check out the documentation above for the latest updates!\n- LLMs are a phenomenal piece of technology for knowledge generation and reasoning. They are pre-trained on large amounts of publicly available data.\n- How do we best augment LLMs with our own private data?\nWe need a comprehensive toolkit to help perform this data augmentation for LLMs.\nThat's where LlamaIndex comes in. LlamaIndex is a \"data framework\" to help you build LLM apps. It provides the following tools:",
    "character_count": 929
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3efe16a1-8eb0-468d-80d0-7344a6d194dd",
    "technology": "Sentence-Based Chunking",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-based-chunking",
    "category": "chunking",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/run-llama/llama_index",
    "path": "sentence_based_chunking/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "That's where LlamaIndex comes in. LlamaIndex is a \"data framework\" to help you build LLM apps. It provides the following tools:\n- Offers data connectors to ingest your existing data sources and data formats (APIs, PDFs, docs, SQL, etc.).\n- Provides ways to structure your data (indices, graphs) so that this data can be easily used with LLMs.\n- Provides an advanced retrieval/query interface over your data: Feed in any LLM input prompt, get back retrieved context and knowledge-augmented output.\n- Allows easy integrations with your outer application framework (e.g. with LangChain, Flask, Docker, ChatGPT, or anything else).\nLlamaIndex provides tools for both beginner users and advanced users. Our high-level API allows beginner users to use LlamaIndex to ingest and query their data in 5 lines of code. Our lower-level APIs allow advanced users to customize and extend any module (data connectors, indices, retrievers, query engines, reranking modules), to fit their needs.",
    "character_count": 977
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d04c4854-249c-4b04-8ec7-da77da878203",
    "technology": "Sentence-Based Chunking",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-based-chunking",
    "category": "chunking",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/run-llama/llama_index",
    "path": "sentence_based_chunking/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "Interested in contributing? Contributions to LlamaIndex core as well as contributing integrations that build on the core are both accepted and highly encouraged! See our Contribution Guide for more details.\nNew integrations should meaningfully integrate with existing LlamaIndex framework components. At the discretion of LlamaIndex maintainers, some integrations may be declined.\nFull documentation can be found here\nPlease check it out for the most up-to-date tutorials, how-to guides, references, and other resources!\n# custom selection of integrations to work with core\npip install llama-index-core\npip install llama-index-llms-openai\npip install llama-index-llms-ollama\npip install llama-index-embeddings-huggingface\nExamples are in the docs/examples folder. Indices are in the indices folder (see list of indices below).\nTo build a simple vector store index using OpenAI:\nimport os\nos.environ[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"] = \"YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY\"",
    "character_count": 940
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "839ca717-e1c5-4bb9-b73f-3bc594210dc6",
    "technology": "Sentence-Based Chunking",
    "technology_id": "source-sentence-based-chunking",
    "category": "chunking",
    "organization": "LlamaIndex",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
