    "chunk_id": "70c7e9da-7f75-4ac6-b96d-16019756b3e6",
    "technology": "Tree of Thoughts (ToT)",
    "technology_id": "source-tree-of-thoughts",
    "category": "prompting",
    "organization": "Independent Research",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm",
    "path": "tree_of_thoughts_tot/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Official implementation for paper Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models with code, prompts, model outputs. Also check its tweet thread in 1min.\n-\nSet up OpenAI API key and store in environment variable OPENAI_API_KEY (see here).\n-\nInstall tot package in two ways:\n- Option 1: Install from PyPI\npip install tree-of-thoughts-llm\n- Option 2: Install from source\ngit clone https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm\ncd tree-of-thought-llm\npip install -r requirements.txt\npip install -e . # install `tot` package\nThe following minimal script will attempt to solve the game of 24 with 4 5 6 10 (might be a bit slow as it's using GPT-4):\nimport argparse\nfrom tot.methods.bfs import solve\nfrom tot.tasks.game24 import Game24Task",
    "character_count": 764
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b4154956-defe-4412-bb70-8df091f364a4",
    "technology": "Tree of Thoughts (ToT)",
    "technology_id": "source-tree-of-thoughts",
    "category": "prompting",
    "organization": "Independent Research",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm",
    "path": "tree_of_thoughts_tot/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "import argparse\nfrom tot.methods.bfs import solve\nfrom tot.tasks.game24 import Game24Task\nargs = argparse.Namespace(backend='gpt-4', temperature=0.7, task='game24', naive_run=False, prompt_sample=None, method_generate='propose', method_evaluate='value', method_select='greedy', n_generate_sample=1, n_evaluate_sample=3, n_select_sample=5)\ntask = Game24Task()\nys, infos = solve(args, task, 900)\nprint(ys[0])\nAnd the output would be something like (note it's not deterministic, and sometimes the output can be wrong):\n10 - 4 = 6 (left: 5 6 6)\n5 * 6 = 30 (left: 6 30)\n30 - 6 = 24 (left: 24)\nAnswer: (5 * (10 - 4)) - 6 = 24\nRun experiments via sh scripts/{game24, text, crosswords}/{standard_sampling, cot_sampling, bfs}.sh, except in crosswords we use a DFS algorithm for ToT, which can be run via scripts/crosswords/search_crosswords-dfs.ipynb.\nThe very simple run.py implements the ToT + BFS algorithm, as well as the naive IO/CoT sampling. Some key arguments:",
    "character_count": 959
  },
  {
