  {
    "chunk_id": "debfd726-c4c7-46ff-a948-e5e5e773457a",
    "technology": "TruLens",
    "technology_id": "source-trulens",
    "category": "evaluation",
    "organization": "TruEra",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/truera/trulens",
    "path": "trulens/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "TruLens finds where your agent fails and where you can cut cost without losing quality. Open source, OpenTelemetry-native.\nInstrument any app with a decorator, score every step with LLM judges that explain themselves, then compare versions and ship the one that earns it. Tracing is OpenTelemetry-native, so a trace is portable to any OTLP backend, and evaluations run either as traces land or over a dataset after the fact.\nRead more about the core concepts behind TruLens including Metrics, the RAG Triad, and Honest, Harmless and Helpful Evals.\nLatency, inputs, outputs, tokens and cost, recorded per step, so a bad answer has a traceable cause rather than a vibe.\nScores, latency and cost per app version, so the tradeoff is visible instead of guessed. The cheapest version is often not the worst one.\nTruLens judges are graded against human annotations, out of the box.\n| Result | Metric | Detail |\n|---|---|---|",
    "character_count": 917
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "573a257f-44dd-42d5-b51e-496a17eca083",
    "technology": "TruLens",
    "technology_id": "source-trulens",
    "category": "evaluation",
    "organization": "TruEra",
    "license": "MIT",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "url": "https://github.com/truera/trulens",
    "path": "trulens/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "TruLens judges are graded against human annotations, out of the box.\n| Result | Metric | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| 95% | Agent errors caught with Agent GPA on TRAIL/GAIA | 267 of 281 human-annotated errors, against 55% for the baseline trace judge (arXiv:2510.08847) |\n| 0.81 | Groundedness F1 on LLM-AggreFact | Ahead of a fine-tuned proprietary model, Bespoke-MiniCheck-7B, on F1, precision and recall over an 11,000-example holdout (RAG triad benchmarks) |\n| 0.93 | Context relevance NDCG@5 | First of five tools on three of four ranking metrics, ahead of WandB Weave, RAGAS, DeepEval and UpTrain (AIMultiple, 23 March 2026) |\n| 4.2:1 | Context relevance adversarial win-loss | Scored the correct passage over a near-copy with one fact swapped 4.2 times for every reversal, against 3.3:1 for the next best tool (AIMultiple) |\nWalmart Global Tech, Cisco, J.P. Morgan Chase, Equinix, VMware by Broadcom, Hitachi Digital Services, Thomson Reuters, phData, HID Global and others. See ADOPTERS.md.",
    "character_count": 994
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3395a311-9057-4222-a047-9d9292d1e1c9",
    "technology": "TruLens",
    "technology_id": "source-trulens",
    "category": "evaluation",
    "organization": "TruEra",
