    "chunk_index": 13,
    "text": "unsloth studio -p 8888\nTo install into an isolated location (its own virtual env, auth/, studio.db, cache and llama.cpp build), set UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME and pass it again at launch:\n$env:UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=\"$PWD\\.studio\"; .\\install.ps1 --local\n$env:UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=\"$PWD\\.studio\"; unsloth studio -p 8888\nThen to update :\ncd unsloth; git pull\n.\\install.ps1 --local\nunsloth studio -p 8888\nBy default unsloth studio binds to 127.0.0.1 (this machine only). To reach it from another device, pick one of:\n- --secure (recommended): serve only through a free Cloudflare HTTPS link. Unsloth stays bound to localhost and the tunnel provides the public URL; it fails closed (does not start) if the tunnel can't come up, so the raw port is never exposed.\nunsloth studio --secure -p 8888",
    "character_count": 778
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "569b189b-2bf1-4d9c-bc15-f9ea58dfeab4",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
