    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Features • News • Quickstart • Notebooks • Documentation\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | shirm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\nUnsloth Studio (Beta) lets you run and train text, audio, embedding, vision models on Windows, Linux and macOS.\n- Search + download + run models including GGUF, LoRA adapters, safetensors\n- Export models: Save or export models to GGUF, 16-bit safetensors and other formats.\n- Tool calling: Support for self-healing tool calling and web search\n- Code execution: lets LLMs test code in Claude artifacts and sandbox environments\n- API inference endpoint: Deploy and run local LLMs in Claude Code, Codex tools with Unsloth\n- Auto set inference settings and customize chat templates.\n- We work directly with teams behind gpt-oss, Qwen3, Llama 4, Mistral, Gemma 1-3, and Phi-4, where we’ve fixed bugs that improve model accuracy.\n- Chat with images, audio, PDFs, code, DOCX and more. Connect API providers (OpenAI, Anthropic) or servers (vLLM, Ollama).",
    "character_count": 989
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "429bc043-c920-4b20-b7e1-aaa5dc5191ef",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "- Chat with images, audio, PDFs, code, DOCX and more. Connect API providers (OpenAI, Anthropic) or servers (vLLM, Ollama).\n- Compare any two models side by side with the same prompt.\n- OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible APIs: Serve local models through /v1/chat/completions ,/v1/responses and/v1/messages .\n- Connect local models to agents: Use unsloth start with Claude Code, Codex, Hermes and more.\n- Web/PDF search can read PDF papers, manuals and other PDF results.\n- GGUF hardware controls: Choose GPUs/layers, offload MoE experts, use multi-GPU or Tensor Parallelism.\n- The opt-in MCP control endpoint lets AI clients manage models, training, recipes and exports.\n- Train and RL 500+ models up to 2x faster with 70% less VRAM; MoE up to 12x faster.\n- Train and run RL on AMD GPUs across Windows, WSL and Linux.\n- Data Recipes: Auto-create datasets from PDF, CSV, DOCX etc. Edit data in a visual-node workflow.",
    "character_count": 908
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2135f015-f111-4f84-9258-4a236963507b",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "- Train and run RL on AMD GPUs across Windows, WSL and Linux.\n- Data Recipes: Auto-create datasets from PDF, CSV, DOCX etc. Edit data in a visual-node workflow.\n- Reinforcement Learning uses 80% less VRAM for GRPO, FP8 and vision RL, with 7x longer contexts.\n- Long-context training: 3x faster, 30% less VRAM and 500K+ context.\n- Supports LoRA/QLoRA, full fine-tuning, RL, pretraining, 4-bit, 16-bit and FP8.\n- Custom Triton and mathematical kernels built with PyTorch and Hugging Face.\n- Observability: Monitor training live, track loss and GPU usage and customize graphs.\n- Multi-GPU training is supported, with major improvements coming soon.\nUnsloth Start connects Claude Code, Codex and other agents to local models with one command.\nStart Unsloth, load a model, open your project folder, then run:\nunsloth start claude\nReplace claude with any supported agent:\n| Agent | Command |\n|---|---|\n| Claude Code | unsloth start claude |\n| OpenAI Codex | unsloth start codex |",
    "character_count": 973
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ecf2795c-0503-4b2e-ac0e-d2ba188e80bf",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
