    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "text": "- Introducing Unsloth Studio: our new web UI for running and training LLMs. Blog\n- Train MoE LLMs 12x faster with 35% less VRAM - DeepSeek, GLM, Qwen and gpt-oss. Blog\n- Embedding models: Unsloth now supports ~1.8-3.3x faster embedding fine-tuning. Blog • Notebooks\n- New 7x longer context RL vs. all other setups, via our new batching algorithms. Blog\n- New RoPE & MLP Triton Kernels & Padding Free + Packing: 3x faster training & 30% less VRAM. Blog\n- 500K Context: Training a 20B model with >500K context is now possible on an 80GB GPU. Blog\n- FP8 & Vision RL: You can now do FP8 & VLM GRPO on consumer GPUs. FP8 Blog • Vision RL\nThe below advanced instructions are for Unsloth Studio. For Unsloth Core advanced installation, view our docs.\nThe developer install builds from the main branch, which is the latest (nightly) source.\ngit clone https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth\ncd unsloth\n./install.sh --local\nunsloth studio -p 8888",
    "character_count": 934
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e1df728d-21b9-426c-95c9-e1eaf9621313",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "text": "The developer install builds from the main branch, which is the latest (nightly) source.\ngit clone https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth\ncd unsloth\n./install.sh --local\nunsloth studio -p 8888\nTo install into an isolated location (its own virtual env, auth/, studio.db, cache and llama.cpp build), set UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME and pass it again at launch:\nUNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=\"$PWD/.studio\" ./install.sh --local\nUNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=\"$PWD/.studio\" unsloth studio -p 8888\nThen to update :\ncd unsloth && git pull\n./install.sh --local\nunsloth studio -p 8888\nThe developer install builds from the main branch, which is the latest (nightly) source.\ngit clone https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth.git\ncd unsloth\nSet-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass\n.\\install.ps1 --local\nunsloth studio -p 8888\nTo install into an isolated location (its own virtual env, auth/, studio.db, cache and llama.cpp build), set UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME and pass it again at launch:",
    "character_count": 959
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0fe00d37-8352-44e9-8bda-b68a8748e6f7",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "text": "unsloth studio -p 8888\nTo install into an isolated location (its own virtual env, auth/, studio.db, cache and llama.cpp build), set UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME and pass it again at launch:\n$env:UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=\"$PWD\\.studio\"; .\\install.ps1 --local\n$env:UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=\"$PWD\\.studio\"; unsloth studio -p 8888\nThen to update :\ncd unsloth; git pull\n.\\install.ps1 --local\nunsloth studio -p 8888\nBy default unsloth studio binds to 127.0.0.1 (this machine only). To reach it from another device, pick one of:\n- --secure (recommended): serve only through a free Cloudflare HTTPS link. Unsloth stays bound to localhost and the tunnel provides the public URL; it fails closed (does not start) if the tunnel can't come up, so the raw port is never exposed.\nunsloth studio --secure -p 8888",
    "character_count": 778
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "5c8270e1-30e3-4da7-8fdf-0836137437bf",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "text": "unsloth studio --secure -p 8888\n- -H 0.0.0.0 : bind the raw port on all network interfaces, reachable from anywhere on the network (subject to your firewall). It does not create a public internet URL; add--cloudflare to also publish an internet-reachablehttps://*.trycloudflare.com link even behind a firewall. Only use this on a network you trust.\nunsloth studio -H 0.0.0.0 -p 8888\nThe Cloudflare tunnel is off by default: -H 0.0.0.0 exposes the raw port only, not a public internet URL. Pair the wildcard bind with --cloudflare (unsloth studio -H 0.0.0.0 --cloudflare) to also publish a public https://*.trycloudflare.com link, or prefer --secure (above), which keeps the raw port private. --cloudflare has no effect on a loopback bind.",
    "character_count": 738
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "25f5fb4c-0651-4c19-9e22-4bc5d20bbd08",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "text": "On a wildcard bind Unsloth works out the address to share by asking ifconfig.me for the public IP, then asks check-host.net whether that port is reachable so it can tell you if a firewall is in the way. Both contact a third party. Set UNSLOTH_STUDIO_DISABLE_PUBLIC_CHECK=1 to skip them; the banner then shows the LAN address and no reachability line.\nThe first time Unsloth is published on a public URL (--secure or --cloudflare) with the auto-generated admin password still in place, it asks for a new admin password in the terminal (masked input with confirmation) before the public link goes up. Without an attached terminal it warns instead and keeps the bootstrap deadline: Unsloth shuts down after UNSLOTH_STUDIO_BOOTSTRAP_TIMEOUT (default 1 hour) unless the password is changed in the web UI.",
    "character_count": 799
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2acb284d-0a00-4777-8e4f-51312323ad74",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "text": "For headless setups that cannot answer that prompt, set the initial admin password non-interactively with --password (only takes effect when no password is set yet; if one already exists it is a hard error, so rotate later with unsloth studio reset-password):\nunsloth studio --secure --password 'your-strong-password' # visible in `ps`/history\nUNSLOTH_STUDIO_PASSWORD='your-strong-password' unsloth studio --secure # via env var\nprintf '%s\\n' 'your-strong-password' | unsloth studio --secure --password - # via stdin\nA literal --password VALUE is visible in the process list and shell history, so prefer the UNSLOTH_STUDIO_PASSWORD env var or --password - (stdin) for automation. This applies to any launch (public or a headless -H 0.0.0.0 bind), and the password is set in the parent before the server binds, so it never reaches a re-executed child process.",
    "character_count": 858
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ec1a2008-a2cb-46c3-a45e-214b8cfbaaca",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "text": "Server-side tools (web search, Python and terminal code execution) run as your user and are on by default. Anyone who can reach the server with the API key can run code on this machine, so keep your API key private and pass --disable-tools when exposing Unsloth.\nInstaller options can be passed as environment variables. On macOS, Linux and WSL place the variable after the pipe so the shell passes it to sh; on Windows set it with $env: before piping to iex.\nSkip PyTorch (GGUF-only mode):\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | UNSLOTH_NO_TORCH=1 sh$env:UNSLOTH_NO_TORCH=1; irm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\nSkip the post-install prompt that starts Unsloth (useful for automated installs):\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | UNSLOTH_SKIP_AUTOSTART=1 sh$env:UNSLOTH_SKIP_AUTOSTART=1; irm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\nPin the Python version:",
    "character_count": 868
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b6a22db5-b5d6-4dc2-85b0-2818e1007c97",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "text": "curl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | UNSLOTH_SKIP_AUTOSTART=1 sh$env:UNSLOTH_SKIP_AUTOSTART=1; irm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\nPin the Python version:\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | UNSLOTH_PYTHON=3.12 sh$env:UNSLOTH_PYTHON='3.12'; irm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\nInstall to a custom location with UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME:\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME=/abs/path sh$env:UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME='C:\\path'; irm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\nOn macOS, the installer defaults to the system certificate store (UV_SYSTEM_CERTS=1) so uv trusts the CAs in your Keychain, needed behind TLS-inspecting proxies (Cisco Umbrella, Zscaler, etc.). Opt out with:\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | UV_SYSTEM_CERTS=0 sh\nPoint the frontend build at a corporate npm mirror/proxy with UNSLOTH_NPM_REGISTRY (for the developer install behind a firewall that blocks registry.npmjs.org):",
    "character_count": 939
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "0277c626-bf5a-4fd9-9508-1901daac9ebd",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
    "technology_id": "source-unsloth",
    "category": "fine_tuning",
    "organization": "Unsloth AI",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "priority": "high",
    "update_frequency": "weekly",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "url": "https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/README.md",
    "path": "unsloth/official_documentation.json",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "text": "Point the frontend build at a corporate npm mirror/proxy with UNSLOTH_NPM_REGISTRY (for the developer install behind a firewall that blocks registry.npmjs.org):\nUNSLOTH_NPM_REGISTRY=https://artifactory.example.com/api/npm/npm/ ./install.sh --local$env:UNSLOTH_NPM_REGISTRY='https://artifactory.example.com/api/npm/npm/'; .\\install.ps1 --local\nIt is threaded as --registry into the Unsloth frontend npm/bun installs; the supply-chain locks (7-day min-release-age, exact version pins) stay in force.\nCap Unsloth's native CPU thread pools on high-core hosts: UNSLOTH_CPU_THREADS=8 unsloth studio -p 8888.\nThe recommended way to fully remove Unsloth Studio is the matching uninstall script for your OS. It stops any running servers, removes the install dir, the launcher data dir, the desktop shortcut, and any platform-specific entries (macOS .app bundle + Launch Services on Mac; Start Menu, HKCU\\Software\\Unsloth registry key and user PATH entries on Windows):",
    "character_count": 959
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "bfa4a6d6-9699-47df-8edb-22facd7619e0",
    "technology": "Unsloth",
