    "path": "weaviate/github_repository.json",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Weaviate is an open-source, cloud-native vector database that stores both objects and vectors, enabling semantic search at scale. It combines vector similarity search with keyword filtering, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and reranking in a single query interface. Common use cases include RAG systems, semantic and image search, recommendation engines, chatbots, and content classification.\nWeaviate supports two approaches to store vectors: automatic vectorization at import using integrated models (OpenAI, Cohere, HuggingFace, and others) or direct import of pre-computed vector embeddings. Production deployments benefit from built-in multi-tenancy, replication, RBAC authorization, and many other features.\nTo get started quickly, have a look at one of these tutorials:\nWeaviate offers multiple installation and deployment options:\nSee the installation docs for more deployment options, such as AWS and GCP.\nYou can easily start Weaviate and a local vector embedding model with Docker.",
    "character_count": 998
  },
